\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ leaves market surplus, sterilising  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1999\par 01:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Dec 1 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it left the money market with a projected net surplus of 1.0 trillion yen on Wednesday, effectively sterilising its yen selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The surplus amount was unchanged from the level left after the BOJ's Tuesday's \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At its regular 0020 GMT money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered to sell 100 billion yen worth of bills through an auction, absorbing the excess funds it created through its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales on Monday. \par \par \uc2  As a result, the net projected surplus in the money market on Wednesday was 1.0 trillion yen, it said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  Money traders said the BOJ's stance to leave the net surplus in the money market unchanged from the previous day indicates that it sterilised - or drained excess yen funds created by - the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it had conducted on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ, acting as the government's agent, repeatedly sold yen on Monday to buy dollars and euros, lifting the dollar as high as 104.08 yen from a low of 102.30 yen. \par \par \uc2  Settlements on the BOJ's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday will occur on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc108zlw\par }\page {\