\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  - Euro dips back under $1.01, eyes precipice. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 614 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1999\par 12:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 1 (Reuters) - The euro dipped below $1.01 and dropped against the yen by the European midsession on Wednesday, after failing to gain long-term support from strong euro-zone economic reports. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said euro-zone manufacturing purchasing managers' surveys released on Wednesday were not enough to lure investors back into the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with the year-end only one month away. \par \par \uc2  "It's not really about European or U.S. fundamentals," said David Coleman, chief economist at CIBC World Markets. \par \par \uc2  "It's Y2K-related - investors are looking to diversify into the most liquid areas, and the most liquid is the U.S. market." \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading just below $1.01 EUR=) at 1105 GMT, a little over half a cent above the lifetime low of $1.0034 hit on Monday. The euro was around 1.3 yen above an all-time low of 102.13 yen EURJPY=) set earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  The Reuters Eurozone Purchasing Managers' Index for manufacturing gave a reading of 57.0 in November, matching its 18-month high set in October. \par \par \uc2  French manufacturing and output hit record levels in November, and the German manufacturing PMI inched to 55.33 in November, the fastest rate of expansion since July, 1998. \par \par \uc2  But analysts and dealers said the euro's failure to break above key resistance at $1.0150, coupled with the failure of the Swiss franc to appreciate beyond 1.58 to the dollar, kept the outlook sickly for the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "As long as we stay below $1.0150, the downside is still in focus," said a dealer from a German bank in Frankfurt. \par \par \uc2  "Our traders are looking for new lows, and for parity," he added. \par \par \uc2  MARKET EYES DIRECT, VERBAL \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  The yen fluctuated in a half-yen range against the dollar and a one-yen range against the euro, with major market moves likely to hinge on comments from Japanese officials, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Traders detected no sign of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia after its forays into the market on Monday and Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said dollar/yen JPY=) could weaken later as people were sceptical about the effectivness of Japan's action to curb yen strength. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading above 102 yen, around one yen yen above last week's four-year low. \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Wednesday, the dollar received a slight boost after an ambiguous statement by BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami prompted speculation of a further easing in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  But money market data showing that the BOJ had effectively sterilised its yen selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday quashed such talk and forced the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to give up much of its modest gains. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 1103 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at \par \par \uc2  2130GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par .\tab \tab \tab     Last     US Close  % Chg   YTD %   1998\par .\tab \tab \tab \tab \tab  30 Nov\tab \tab \tab   Close\par \par .\tab \tab \tab     -----------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr\tab \tab     1.0089   1.0089   +0.00   -13.92   1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab      102.66   102.12   +0.53   -13.92   113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab     103.58   103.04   +0.52    -9.31   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.5857   1.5871   -0.09   +15.45   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.6005   1.5984   +0.13    -3.23   1.6539\par Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4735   1.4736   -0.01    -3.66   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6364   0.6351   +0.20    +4.07   0.6115\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.6005   1.6022   -0.11    -0.71   1.6119\par Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6296   0.6305   -0.14   -10.33   0.7021\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc108tse\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
