\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro propped, but parity still in sight. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 739 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Dezember 1999\par 09:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Dec 1 (Reuters) - The euro held about a cent away from the psychological one-for-one rate against the dollar on Wednesday, mildly supported by strong euro-zone economic reports. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said a batch of purchasing managers' index surveys coming out of France, Germay and the euro zone on Wednesday morning should keep the euro propped above its lows for the time being despite its proximity with parity with the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  The French manufacturing and output PMI for November hit record levels. The German survey and a euro-zone report due out later today are also expected to be supportive for the euro. "The PMIs are coming out of Europe this morning should all be fairly strong while as far as the dollar is concerned there may be some nerves about the NAPM survey this afternoon, particularly the price component," said Jeremy Hawkins, chief economic advisor at Bank of America in London. "The numbers on the whole for once should be in favour of the euro. The question is whether they are going to be sufficiently robust to turn around the current bearish euro sentiment." \par \par \uc2  The euro stood just above $1.01, more than half cent above the lifetime low of $1.0034 hit on Monday. The euro was more than a yen above an all-time low of 102.13 yen set earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the euro's decline had yet to elicit strong protest from European policymakers, probably because of the competitive edge it was giving European exporters. \par \par \uc2  "The Europeans are generally pretty comfortable about the euro at these sort of levels and European exporters are thrilled," said James Shugg, economist at Westpac in London. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think it is such a problem that the euro is at these levels." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  FEARS STILL LINGER \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the dollar was propped above its lows against the euro after traders detected no sign of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia after its forays into the market on Monday and Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said dollar/yen could weaken later as people were sceptical against the effectivness of Japan's action to curb yen strength. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trading above 102 yen, more than half yen above last week's four-year low of 101.22. \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Wednesday, the dollar had received a slight boost after an ambiguous statement by BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami prompted speculation of a further easing in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  But money market data showing that the BOJ had effectively sterilised its yen selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday quashed such talk and forced the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to give up much of its modest gains. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that they have decided to sterilise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  means that nothing has rally changed," said Hawkins at Bank of America. \par \par \uc2  "If the BOJ were serious about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen then they would leave the money in the money market. So it appears there's been no change in policy. People who were buying the yen before will still be inclined to buy yen." \par \par \uc2  Looking forward, dealers said they expected the yen to gain more ground against the dollar in coming weeks. \par \par \uc2  The release next Monday of July-September gross domestic product data, and of the BOJ's "tankan" corporate survey the following week, could be catalysts for the dollar's fall below 100 yen, said Yasuharu Tsuru, manager for Mitsubishi Trust and Banking Corp in Tokyo. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0819 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 \par \par \uc2  GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par .\tab \tab \tab  Last     US Close  % Chg   YTD %  1998 Close\par .\tab \tab \tab \tab     30 Nov.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par --------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab  1.0100   1.0089   +0.11   -13.83   1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab   102.18   102.12   +0.06   -13.83   113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab  103.24   103.04   +0.19    -9.73   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab 1.5851   1.5871   -0.13   +15.41   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab   1.5977   1.5984   -0.04    -3.40   1.6539\par Can/dlr\tab \tab   1.4735   1.4736   -0.01    -3.66   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab   0.6380   0.6351   +0.46    +4.33   0.6115\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/swiss  1.6017   1.6022   -0.03    -0.63   1.6119\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/stg\tab \tab  0.6322   0.6305   +0.27    -9.96   0.7021\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvc108trw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
