\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ also bought euros for yen on Tuesday - bankers. \b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 1999\par 09:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 30 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (BOJ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets late in Tokyo trade on Tuesday included buying of euros for yen, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda confirmed late on Tuesday afternoon that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for a second consecutive day to curb the yen's strength. He declined to comment, however, on whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  included buying of euros for yen. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buoyed by the BOJ's apparent euro-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , jumped to nearly 104 yen from its intraday Tokyo low around 102.30 yen, which has barely above a lifetime low of 102.28 yen marked in New York on Friday. \par \par \uc2  But yen-buying interest by Japanese institutional investors remained solid on Tuesday, limiting any gains in the euro as well as in the dollar, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  As of 0740 GMT, the euro was quoted at 103.31/38 yen, compared with 103.37 late in New York on Monday. The BOJ, acting as an agent of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , conducted yen-selling, dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly in Tokyo on Monday, briefly boosting the dollar above 104 yen. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also included euro buying for the yen. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday morning, Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa appeared to acknowledge that Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  included euro buying. \par \par \uc2  Asked by reporters why \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought both euros and dollars for yen on Monday, Miyazawa said: "There was no special reason. It's just that the euro's weak." ((Risa Maeda, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-3432-8570 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbu095ex\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
