\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ seen buying dlrs intermittently around Y102.50. \b0\par\par\uc2 213 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 1999\par 08:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 30 (Reuters) - The Bank of Japan (BOJ) was detected buying dollars intermittently from around 102.50 yen in late afternoon Tokyo trade on Tuesday, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was spotted stepping in to buy dollars for yen from about the time the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped to the day's low around 101.33 yen in late afternoon. \par \par \uc2  BOJ bids appeared to have been prominent especially after the dollar rose to around 102 yen, one banker said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ acts as an agent of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, conducting actual dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The BOJ sold yen for dollars repeatedly in Tokyo on Monday, briefly boosting the dollar above 104 yen, but the dollar later came under heavy pressure in overseas markets. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said on Tuesday morning that he was not satisfied with current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Japan's Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs, Haruhiko Kuroda, declined to comment on whether \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  As of 0718 GMT, the dollar stood at 102.85/95 yen. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432-8785 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbu095cq\par }\page {\pa