\par\par \b \uc2  Bundesbank seen buying euro, but orders commercial. \b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 1999\par 12:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 30 (Reuters) - Bundesbank orders to buy euros for sterling were behind a sharp spike up in the euro on Tuesday but the transactions were likely to have been for commercial purposes, people familiar with the bank's activities said. \par \par \uc2  Rumours had earlier swirled around the foreign exchanges that purchases of euros for pounds were being conducted on behalf of a European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with several German banks reported to have bought euros from about 63.10 pence up to about 63.30. \par \par \uc2  The Bundesbank and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment. The Bank of England also declined to comment on sterling's move and the talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  activity. \par \par \uc2  But bankers familiar with the Bundesbank's activities said the orders were likely to be connected to month-end \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  typically conducted by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  but had had a big impact because the foreign exchanges were primed for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  While central banks' reserve management requires them to buy and sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of their everyday activities, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers become more sensitive to such orders when their timing seems to coincide with exchange rates approaching key levels. \par \par \uc2  On several occasions over the past decade the Bundesbank has been seen operating on the foreign exchanges after extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves but ostensibly executing commercial orders. \par \par \uc2  The foreign exchanges are particularly alert to the risks of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in more than two months on Monday and sold yen again during Asian trading on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Wariness is also rife that European central banks could step in to halt a slide which has taken the euro to life lows within half a cent of parity against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  ((Swaha Pattanaik, London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6284, swaha.pattanaik@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbu094zi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
