\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ did not  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  for month to Friday - bankers. \b0\par\par\uc2 236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 1999\par 11:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 30 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) conducted no yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for a one-month period to last Friday, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  Data released by the BOJ on Tuesday showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) paid 5.0 billion yen to the private sector during the month through its special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account. \par \par \uc2  The MOF has confirmed that the BOJ, acting as an agent of the ministry, conducted yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday and Tuesday, but settlements of the ministry's yen sales are made two days after transactions and are not included in Tuesday's data. \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the ministry's payments to the private sector during the month were almost negligible, marking a sharp contrast with the ministry's payments worth 1.05 trillion yen in September when the BOJ last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The MOF's special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account is used mainly to fund \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted by the BOJ. Disbursements also include financial transactions between Japan and global institutions such as the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  The figures include the last two trading days of the previous month, but not the last two business days of the month, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlements are made two days after transactions. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-3432-8570 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbu094wf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
