\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ seen sterilising  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2  - traders. \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 1999\par 11:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 30 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) is expected to sterilise the yen created by Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , money market dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades settle on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ, acting as the government's agent, repeatedly sold yen on Monday to buy dollars and euros, lifting the dollar as high as 104.08 yen from a low of 102.30 yen. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said the BOJ had already taken steps to absorb the excess funds created by Monday's yen sales. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ on Tuesday offered to sell a total of 1.4 trillion yen worth of discount bills via an auction starting on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to absorb excess yen funds, although it's difficult to say if this amount is the actual size of the BOJ's action," a senior money dealer at a major city bank said. \par \par \uc2  According to the BOJ's fund supply/demand projections, it expects a net surplus of 1.06 trillion yen in the money market on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Money market participants expect the BOJ will drain 100 billion yen from the market at its regular 0020 GMT \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  to leave a net surplus, as usual, of around 1.0 trillion yen. \par \par \uc2  If the key overnight call rate shows signs of rising sharply, the BOJ could leave a larger surplus. \par \par \uc2  But that would not indicate unsterilised action or additional monetary easing, but rather a determination to continue targeting short-term interest rates at zero, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  As part of this policy, which the BOJ's Policy Board reaffirmed last Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been leaving the money market with a net surplus of one trillion yen after its morning \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ((Tamawa Kadoya, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbu094fq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
