\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen sneaks higher despite Japan warnings. \b0\par\par\uc2 806 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 1999\par 05:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 30 (Reuters) - The yen was on the attack again by Tokyo midday on Tuesday, with only Japanese threats of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  keeping the dollar propped up around the 102 level. \par \par \uc2  Despite a chorus of warnings by Tokyo officials, the dollar sank to below levels where the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday to curb its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength. \par \par \uc2  In the strongest hint of further official action, Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa said he was not satisfied with current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels and that Japan would step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at any time if necessary. \par \par \uc2  But speculators were betting that Japan would get little or no help from Europe or the United States in its efforts to cap the yen, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar is held at around 102 yen because people are expecting \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any time," said a European bank dealer. "But many seem eager to see the dollar fall below that level in order to buy on dips," he said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par As of 0225 GMT, the dollar\tab   was quoted at 102.05/15 yen, compared with 102.33 yen in late New York on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said they had not spotted yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the BOJ which, as an agent of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , conducted yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  repeatedly in Tokyo on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said yen buying was partly fuelled by Miyazawa's comments on Tuesday that there would be no joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at present.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Miyazawa told reporters as he left a cabinet meeting that the possibility of joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would depend on market developments.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asked about the possibility of such a move, Miyazawa said: "That will depend on how things develop." But he added: "Not now."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Asked why Japan bought both euros and dollars for yen on Monday, Miyazawa said: "There was no special reason, it's just that the euro's weak."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He later said European authorities did not seem to think the euro's current levels were a problem.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We understand this is going to be an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to smooth out disruptive market moves. But if they want to alarm the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market into realising that the moves have been excessive, more aggressive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is necessary," said the European bank trader.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The yen has been supported by a brightening outlook for the Japanese economy, although consumer spending remains sluggish.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Given growing concern that the 11-nation euro zone is making only sluggish progress in reforming its economies and companies, the yen appears to have the potential to strengthen further, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro was quoted at 103.08/16 yen\tab     , compared with 103.37 in late New York on Monday.\par Against the dollar, the euro was at $1.0102/12\tab   by 0350 GMT, little changed from $1.0093 in New York.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders also said expectations for an increase in direct foreign investment in Japan are strong after Monday's announcement that French insurer AXA  would take control of unlisted medium-sized Japanese insurer Nippon Dantai Life Insurance Co by setting up Japan's first insurance holding company.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The euro seems to still be under attack against the yen against the backdrop of increased investment from Europe, either directly or by buying Japanese stocks," said a Japanese trust bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Such optimistic views on Japan were echoed by Economic Planning Agency (EPA) Minister Taichi Sakaiya, who said on Tuesday that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  levels set by the market may have to be accepted in the long term.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The reason the yen has been rising is increased optimism over Japan's economy," Sakaiya told reporters at a regular news conference. "The economy is resilient," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Some dealers said active yen buying since Friday seems to have been overdone as it was accelerated by buying ahead of the year-end by Japanese exporters and institutional investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The recent rally was bolstered by yen buybacks by Japanese exporters and investors mainly in crosses," said a foreign bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "They seemed to be in a hurry to hedge their short euro positions or just make outright yen purchases, mainly due to concerns about the millennium computer bug problem. But if you pause and look at the fundamentals, you would be hesitant to buy (yen) further from the current levels," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday's Japanese economic data confirmed still weak consumer spending and showed the jobless rate in October unchanged from the previous month at 4.6 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Spending by Japanese wage earners' households fell a real 2.4 percent in October from a year earlier to an average 333,401 yen, the Japanese government said on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The spending has fallen from year-earlier levels for nine of the past 13 months, dogged by weak personal incomes. ((Risa Maeda, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-3432-8570 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbu093fr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
