\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen recovers from post- \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  lows. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 694 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 1999\par 09:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 30 (Reuters) - The yen recovered losses seen in Asia as the market shrugged off the latest bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Japanese authorities to limit its gains on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Confirmation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's strength came from senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Haruhiko Kuroda who said he was concerned that the recent drastic rise in the yen could hurt the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  Analysts were sceptical that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  hoped to achieve much directly through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but were rather acting to impress upon the Bank of Japan the need for further measures. \par \par \uc2  "In a sense this is just a track around the course as far as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is concerned and the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets are treating it the same as well. They are reacting to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and then just putting it straight back again afterwards," said Francis Breedon, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Lehman Brothers. \par \par \uc2  "We will watch more for the interaction between the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the BOJ rather than for the interaction between \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the markets because that is really where this is heading. Not even the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  believe they can turn the market around just through normal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dollar/yen\tab   shed more than half a yen from Asian highs above 103 and was just over one percent away from four-year lows around 101.25 set on Friday. That rebound in the yen had brought euro/yen three-quarters of a yen off its Asian peak and around one yen above 102.23 life lows set on Monday. Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa tried to sound resolute, declaring that Japan would step into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets at any time if necessary. But he also conceded that there was little prospect of joint \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  with the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  saying that the European authorities did not think current euro levels were problematic.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The relaxed stance of the ECB was a real headache for the BOJ since much of the upward pressure on the yen was originating in the euro/yen cross. Not only were Japanese institutions hedging their euro debt exposure but offshore investors were switching from euro assets to those in Japan.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Breedon at Lehman said the reluctance of the ECB to act in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets was meant the focus was switching back to dollar/yen and away from euro/yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were probably a bit disappointed not to get any support out of the ECB and so have gone back to the more traditional dollar/yen," he said, adding that would not deter Japan from considering action on euro/yen in the future.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Neither did dealers see much chance of the U.S. extending a helping hand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This is a case of yen strength and euro weakness - it's not a dollar problem," said the U.S. bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Federal Reserve would be unconcerned since the dollar was not weak - it is close to decade highs in trade-weighted terms - and was thus not a threat to U.S. domestic inflation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thus the dollar's fall to four-year lows on the yen around 101.25 yen this week was balanced by a rise to lifetime highs on the euro around $1.0034 and a decade peak on the Swiss franc\tab   at 1.5975 francs.\par Euro/dollar\tab   was more than half a cent away from that life low although it had not managed to keep a grasp on its highs for the day above $1.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said parity for euro/dollar was still on the cards, was just a question of when.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There is almost too clear a (down) trend and the market will want to make it a little bit more difficult than that," said Lehman's Breedon. "It does look like it will get there but probably out of the blue on a day when we don't really expect it." ((London capital markets, +44 171 542 7792, fax +44 171 542 5285, deepthi.wickremasinghe@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbu09354\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
