\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Volatile euro clings just above $1.0. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 796 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 1999\par 14:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 30 (Reuters) - The euro held just above record lows against the dollar and the psychological $1.0 level in volatile trade on Tuesday, with swings exaggerated by persistent talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  following another bout of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  yen sales in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Tuesday the euro had racked up around a quarter of a cent against the dollar and jumped against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid rumours that euros were being purchased for pounds on behalf of a European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , possibly the Bundesbank. \par \par \uc2  It retreated again after European leaders said they were not concerned about prevailing euro exchange rates, but market nervousness about the central banks remained. \par \par \uc2  Remarks by Bundesbak's council member Klaus-Dieter Kuehbacher on the possibility of euro/dollar firming to $1.08 early next year brought further relief to the euro, lifting it above $1.01 and near 103 yen. \par \par \uc2  "The euro has come back with these Kuhebacher comments, the market is a little overshort for the moment," said a trader at a European bank in London. \par \par \uc2  Traders said thin liquidity and the proximity to euro/dollar parity was helping to exaggerate price movements. \par \par \uc2  "In these conditions one cannot exclude that speculators can 'abuse' the tense situation of the market and fake some \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , going aggressively on the market and selling right after that," said a trader at a German bank. \par \par \uc2  The euro was more than half a cent above the life lows it plumbed on Monday at $1.0034. Euro/yen was 3/4 yen above an all-time low of 102.23 hit on Monday while euro/sterling was half a penny up from last week's life low of 62.62 pence. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  VIGIL CONTINUES \par \par \uc2  Dealers remained on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alert after repeated BOJ yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday and Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the fact that the euro was being pushed towards all-time lows against the yen only hours after the most recent BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was a sign that the Japanese bank had been ineffective in curbing yen strength and could only hope to smooth the trend. \par \par \uc2  "The driving force behind the yen strength is the appetite for Japanese assets," said Stewart Newnham, senior strategist at State Street Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "The yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not entirely credible because it is not changing what the market thinks of Japan, therefore it is ineffective. They are leaning against the wind. All the BOJ can do is to dampen the uptrend. It's the most they can hope for." \par \par \uc2  Senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Haruhiko Kuroda confirmed on Tuesday the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia to contain yen strength and said he was concerned that the recent drastic yen rise could hurt Japan's economy. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the market was now focusing on the possibility of joint ECB-BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , maybe on euro/yen, although the European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedely said it is not concerned about prevailing \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. \par \par \uc2  "After the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight and with the euro currently so weak everyone is thinking: is the ECB going to do it or not?," said Ryan Shea, economist at Bank One in London. \par \par \uc2  "There is a possibility that the BOJ will ask the ECB to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the euro, but we don't think the ECB is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on their own behalf yet." \par \par \uc2  Nor did dealers see much chance of the U.S. extending a helping hand. \par \par \uc2  "This is a case of yen strength and euro weakness - it's not a dollar problem," said the U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The Federal Reserve would be unconcerned since the dollar was not weak. It is close to decade highs in trade-weighted terms and not a threat to U.S. domestic inflation. \par \par \uc2  ((London Capital Markets, 0171 542 6745, elisabetta.jucca@reuters.com)). \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 1313GMT.  All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at \par \par \uc2  2130GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par .\tab \tab \tab Last\tab  US Close   %Chg   YTD%   1998 Close\par .\tab \tab \tab \tab      29 Nov.\par .\tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0098   1.0093   +0.05   -13.85   1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     101.95   102.33   -0.37   -13.85   113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    103.17   103.37   -0.19    -9.94   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5849   1.5875   -0.16   +15.39   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.5964   1.6064   -0.62    -3.48   1.6539\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4719   1.4734   -0.10    -3.77   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6340   0.6371   -0.49    +3.68   0.6115\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6021   1.6034   -0.08    -0.61   1.6119\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6321   0.6279   +0.67    -9.97   0.7021\par \f28 \par \pa