\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro firms as  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  nerves resurface. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 779 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 1999\par 12:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 30 (Reuters) - The euro leapt more than a quarter of a cent against the dollar on Tuesday and jumped against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  action resurfaced after repeated Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia. \par \par \uc2  Traders said rumours swirled around the foreign exchanges that euros were being purchased for pounds on behalf of a European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some said the Bundesbank. \par \par \uc2  But they added that the orders were likely to have been commercial in nature and no overt \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been detected. \par \par \uc2  Dealers had been on alert for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the BOJ entered the market for the first time in more than two months on Monday and sold yen again in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday. They said the market was extremely jittery. \par \par \uc2  "In these conditions one cannot exclude that speculators can 'abuse' the tense situation of the market and fake some \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , going aggressively on the market and selling right after that," said a trader at a German bank. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose as high as $1.0144 by 1020 GMT according to Reuters data, more than a cent above the life lows it plumbed on Monday at $1.0034. Euro/sterling rose to peaks of 63.41 pence, up from last week's life low of 62.62 pence. \par \par \uc2  The latest euro leap forced the yen to retreat from session peaks near 102.40, while the dollar rose above 102 against the yen. \par \par \uc2  Senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official Haruhiko Kuroda confirmed on Tuesday the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia to contain yen strength and said he was concerned that the recent drastic yen rise could hurt \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Asia had lifted the dollar to a high of 103 yen from lows near its Friday's 101.22 four-year low and assisted the euro up to around 104 yen, more than 1.5 yen above its Monday all-time low at 102.23. \par \par \uc2  MARKET WONDERING WHETER ECB WILL \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENE\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Analysts said the market was now focusing on the possibility of a joint ECB-BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , maybe on euro/yen, although the European \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedely stated that it is not concerned by prevailing \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate levels. \par \par \uc2  "After the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight and with the euro currently so weak everyone is thinking: is the ECB going to do it or not?," said Ryan Shea, economist at Bank One in London \par \par \uc2  "There is a possibility that the BOJ will ask the ECB to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the euro, but we don't think the ECB is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on their own behalf yet." \par \par \uc2  The relaxed stance of the ECB was a real headache for the BOJ since much of the upward pressure on the yen was originating in the euro/yen cross. \par \par \uc2  Francis Breedon, senior exchange strategist at Lehman Brothers in London, said the reluctance of the ECB to act in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets meant the focus was switching back to dollar/yen and away from euro/yen. \par \par \uc2  "The (Japanese) \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  were probably a bit disappointed not to get any support out of the ECB and so have gone back to the more traditional dollar/yen," he said, adding that this would not deter Japan from considering action on euro/yen in the future. \par \par \uc2  Nor did dealers see much chance of the U.S. extending a helping hand. \par \par \uc2  "This is a case of yen strength and euro weakness - it's not a dollar problem," said the U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The Federal Reserve would be unconcerned since the dollar was not weak - it is close to decade highs in trade-weighted terms - and was thus not a threat to U.S. domestic inflation. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 1135GMT.  All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at \par \par \uc2  2130GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par .\tab \tab    Last     US Close  % Chg   YTD %   1998 Close\par .\tab \tab \tab \tab 29 Nov.\par .\tab \tab     -----------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr\tab \tab     1.0114   1.0093   +0.21   -13.71  1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab      102.04   102.33   -0.28   -13.71  113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab     103.18   103.37   -0.18    -9.86   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.5826   1.5875   -0.31   +15.22   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.5988   1.6064   -0.47    -3.33   1.6539\par Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4729   1.4734   -0.03    -3.70   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6352   0.6371   -0.30    +3.88   0.6115\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.6014   1.6034   -0.12    -0.65   1.6119\par Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6320   0.6279   +0.65    -9.98   0.7021\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908d