\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Slips Again Vs Yen As BOJ Fails To Show \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nick Shindo \par \uc2 810 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 1999\par 06:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The absence of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  pulled the carpet out from under a dollar recovery in Asia Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The embattled euro lost further ground against the yen, but managed to hold steady against the dollar in thin trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The threat of further Japanese action in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to curb the yen's rise provided the backdrop for the day's trading, especially after the dollar slid back to Y101.63 in overnight trading, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday, buying both the dollar and euro against the yen to curb the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent rapid appreciation. \par \par \uc2  Early remarks by finance minister Kiichi Miyazawa that Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been insufficient boosted the dollar to Y102.87 on short-covering, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Miyazawa described Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  steps as "not enough," and at a later press conference hinted at the possibility of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the future if the yen's rise continues. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not satisfied with current \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels. We're in close contact with other (Group of Seven industrialized) countries on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...we are ready to ask for their cooperation if necessary," Miyazawa said. \par \par \uc2  Yet as the session wore on, the failure of the BOJ to show up in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets bolstered renewed yen-buying from both Japanese and overseas funds, a city bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Many dealers said that joint G7 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains only a distant possibility despite Miyazawa's remarks. \par \par \uc2  "The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears to lack the stomach, while the U.S. is not concerned as the dollar is only slipping against the yen," a senior dealer at a Japanese trust bank said. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y101.80, below Y102.37 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at Y103.35 late Monday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0098, flat from New York's close. The euro was at $1.0115 in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y102.80, down from Y103.37 in New York late Monday. The euro was at Y104.53 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6040, down from $1.6066 in New York late Monday. Sterling was at $1.6020 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  With doubts over the ability of the government to stall the yen's rise through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone, downward pressure on the dollar remains fierce, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Having these concerns in mind, Japanese and overseas institutional investors are selling dollars and euros for yen regardless," the trust bank dealer said earlier in the session. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, late in the session, a renewed wave of yen bullishness led by Japanese and overseas funds sent the euro skidding to a record all-time low of Y102.30, while the dollar fell to Y101.34 at 0557 GMT, just a whisker above Friday's 4-year low. \par \par \uc2  "Even exporters were selling at these low-levels due to a surplus of dollars and euros during end-of-month book-closing," Shuji Takano, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at ABN-Amro Bank in Tokyo said. \par \par \uc2  The yen roaring ahead on all fronts set the scene for more official reaction. \par \par \uc2  According to traders in Tokyo, at around 0600 and 0625 GMT the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen through Japanese trust banks, sending the dollar to around Y102.60 from its intrasession low. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ bought dollars for yen through trust banks and others," said a senior Japanese bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  Vice-finance minister Haruhiko Kuroda later confirmed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, without BOJ buying, the dollar's rally could be short-lived, with strong selling interest in the Y103-104 region, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "I expect both the dollar and euro to lose some ground again in overseas markets later," said ABN's Takano. \par \par \uc2  But losses are seen With the BOJ allegedly lurking behind the scenes, players will be extremely nervous of leaving short positions exposed, traders said. \par \par \uc2  In other late trading, the euro edged lower against the dollar, as market speculation that the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could soon be trading at parity dented earlier strength, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0710 GMT (2:10 am EST), the dollar was quoted at Y102.85, above Y102.37 late Monday in New York. The dollar was at Y103.35 late Monday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0103, above $1.0098 New York late Monday. The euro was at $1.0115 in Tokyo Monday. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y103.91, higher than Y103.37 in New York late Monday. The euro was at Y104.53 in Tokyo late Monday. \par \par \uc2  -By Nick Shindo; 813-5255-2929; nick.shindo@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvbu08656\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
