\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Yen rises vs dollar and euro, stocks open down. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Jonathan Standing \par \uc2 683 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 1999\par 10:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 29 (Reuters) - The yen rose against the dollar and the euro on Monday, rejecting repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while traders waited to see if the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would step in to support the euro. \par \par \uc2  European shares opened lower with the focus on takeover bids in the banking and telecommunications industries. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was about two yen JPY=) above four-year lows around 101.25 set on Friday after an overnight high above 104. Euro/yen was two yen above its life low of 102.41 while euro/dollar was within half a cent of its $1.0073 life low, also set on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Government officials confirmed that the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars against yen for the first time in over two months. The BOJ was seen bidding the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at around 103 yen every time it was pushed down by an array of selling led by Japanese exporters and U.S. banks. \par \par \uc2  Traders also said the effect of the Bank of Japan's move was undermined by perceptions that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not about to join any coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  A senior Bank of France official said a fall below parity with the dollar would be a psychological problem. Earlier, Bundesbank council member Klaus-Dieter Kuehbacher said he did not rule out the euro could reach parity against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Austrian National Bank Governor Klaus Liebscher, a member of the ECB council, said he was not a great supporter of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In the equity markets, Royal Bank of Scotland fell 2.5 percent after it bid 27 billion pounds ($43.3 billion) for National Westminster Bank Plc, countering a raised offer from Bank of Scotland unveiled on Friday. NatWest eased 0.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  The spotlight also remained on Vodafone Airtouch Plc's battle to take over Germany's Mannesmann AG. \par \par \uc2  Mannesmann fell over two percent to 196 euros after it rejected on Sunday Vodafone's hostile bid, which valued the German firm at about $130 billion. Mannesmann said however that it wanted to continue cooperating with its British suitor. Vodafone fell 1.4 percent. \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere in the telecoms sector, KPM Telecom of the Netherlands and Sweden's Telia said they planned to sell their 35 percent stake in Eircom, the Irish telecom operator in line with an EU condition for the merger of Telia with Norway's Telenor. \par \par \uc2  French insurer Axa said it planned to take control of Japanese life insurance firm Nippon Dantai and that it would inject up to 1.3 billion euros into a new holding company formed by the two groups. \par \par \uc2  Weaker S&P stock index futures and Wall Street's mixed close on Friday also weighed on market sentiment, while several European exchanges were vulnerable to profit-taking after chalking up new highs on Friday, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones index closed off 19 points at 10,998.91 on Friday in a short session after Thursday's Thanksgiving Holiday, though the technology-heavy Nasdaq charged to a new record. \par \par \uc2  In Japan the Nikkei 225 index closed 64.23 points or 0.34 percent lower at 18,850.27. \par \par \uc2  European government bond prices were lower in early trade with the focus on the euro. Analysts said the weakness of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would keep pressure on the market, although dealers said some buyers had emerged as yields had risen. \par \par \uc2  "We are going to see a lot of focus both on the yen and the euro," said Toronto Dominion Bank trader Peter Metcalfe. \par \par \uc2  At 0800 GMT, the price of the December Bund future was down 0.08 at 105.34, having touched a low of 105.15. The 10-year cash Bund was yielding 5.234 percent. \par \par \uc2  The markets will be watching euro zone trade figures for August and September, due for release at 1100 GMT. Markets will also be keeping a close eye on Monday's meeting of European Union finance ministers, which ECB President Wim Duisenberg is due to attend. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbt097pn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
