\par\par \b \uc2  LDP Kamei - Japan should urge joint  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  move-Jiji. \b0\par\par\uc2 184 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 1999\par 09:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 29 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  should call for concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to correct the yen's recent rise, Shizuka Kamei, policy chief of the ruling Liberal Democratic Party (LDP), was quoted by Jiji news agency as saying on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Regarding dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities to curb the yen's rise on Monday, Kamei was quoted as saying: "We should urge the world to cooperate." \par \par \uc2  Traders said the Bank of Japan (BOJ) was first detected buying dollars at levels around 103 yen in morning Tokyo trade on Monday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the morning was confirmed by government officials, including Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa, later in the day. \par \par \uc2  In late afternoon trade in Tokyo, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen buying euros for yen after intermittently buying dollars for yen throughout the day, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ acts as an agent of the Finance Ministry and conducts actual dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  through brokers and private banks. ((Tokyo Newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbt097jn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
