\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen reverses losses, scorns  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 547 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 1999\par 12:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 29 (Reuters) - The yen erased losses inflicted by repeated Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday and was seen setting new highs against the dollar and the euro with traders' keen to test central bankers' resolve. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa confirmed earlier in the day that the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during Asian trading to buy dollars against yen for the first time in over two months. \par \par \uc2  But despite several BOJ attempt to lift the dollar every time it approached 103 yen, the U.S \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was pushed back to session lows as comments by European central bankers led the market to think that the BOJ would be left alone in its decision to use market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth disruptive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/yen has come off despite one or two threats coming out of Japan," said a London-based U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  "But until we see the colour of their money in Europe, the market will still try to head where it wants to head." \par \par \uc2  The dollar was within a yen of four-year lows around 101.25 set on Friday having backed off an Asian high above 104. Euro/yen was less than a yen above its life low of 102.41 set on Friday according to Reuters Graphics. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the euro was within half a cent of its $1.0073 life low set on Friday and still within reach of parity against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The euro had started to falter early in Europe after Bundesbank council member Klaus-Dieter Kuehbacher said it could test parity with the dollar on Monday and eased further after ECB's council member Klaus Liebscher was quoted as saying he was "not a great supporter" of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  NEW RECORD LOWS IN SIGHT \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that given the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's apparent reluctance to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , chances were that euro/dollar and euro/yen could head lower. Meanwhile, further dollar/yen losses risked triggering more Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they added. \par \par \uc2  "If we decline below 102 (on dollar/yen), there is a good chance that we will get \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  today once again," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi in London. \par \par \uc2  "The Japanese authorities will do their utmost to protect the 100 level. But under present circumstances it looks like we will go through the 100 level, and that probably means that we will reach parity and 100 in euro/yen." \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on talk from Tokyo bankers that the BOJ was seen buying euros for yen and was not seen taking part in coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to lift the euro against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "Only if the ECB steps in will it impress the markets, but we don't think they will," said Klaus Kusber, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson in Frankfurt. \par \par \uc2  "The ECB is very keen on giving the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets the impression that it has a benign neglect policy. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the market would take a keen interest in ECB President Wim Duisenberg's comments on the euro when he appears before the European Parliament's economic and monetary affairs committee at 1400 GMT. \par \par \uc2  ((Lisa Jucca, London Capital Markets 0171 542 6745, elisabetta.jucca@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbt096ie\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
