\par\par \b \uc2  Miyazawa says  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  can  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  until  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  normal. \b0\par\par\uc2 261 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 1999\par 03:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 29 (Reuters) - Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa confirmed that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Monday, and said the ministry had enough funds to keep doing so until the "situation was normalised." \par \par \uc2  Bankers said the Bank of Japan (BOJ) was detected buying dollars from around 103 yen in early Tokyo trade on Monday. They added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times. \par \par \uc2  "Movements that disturb the markets are not favourable. We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Tokyo market," Miyazawa told reporters. \par \par \uc2  "We have enough money. We will (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) until the situation is normalised," he added. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the possibility of U.S.-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's recent rise, Miyazawa said: "We're now in Tokyo trading time, so Japan would be the first one to take action." \par \par \uc2  Asked about the yen's rise of around three yen per dollar in overseas trading on Friday, Miyazawa told reporters at the entrance of the Finance Ministry: "It was not orderly." \par \par \uc2  The ministry's stance of taking appropriate action in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will remain unchanged, he added. \par \par \uc2  "On Friday, I instructed (my staff) that they can \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if there are disruptive movements," Miyazawa said. \par \par \uc2  "So I assume they took action (based on the instructions)." \par \par \uc2  The BOJ acts as an agent of the ministry and conducts actual dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  through brokers and private banks. ((Tokyo Newsroom +81-3 3432 8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbt0967s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
