\par\par \b \uc2  Weak euro no worry, has room to rise-BOF's Bernard. \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 1999\par 02:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 29 (Reuters) - The recent weakness of the euro reflects differences in the economic cycle and is not a cause for concern as it is not stoking inflation, a senior Bank of France official said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Jean-Rene Bernard, a member of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate-setting Monetary Policy Council, said Europeans had learned not to over react to short-term variations in the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In remarks prepared for delivery to a seminar in Tokyo, Bernard said: "The euro has a potential for appreciation. This is especially true given that internal price stability has been and will be maintained in the euro area." \par \par \uc2  Bernard noted that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has no exchange rate target for the euro, adding: "A certain degree of flexibility is needed in the exchange rate of the euro." \par \par \uc2  He said the only reason why the weakening of the euro would have become a concern for the ECB was if it had translated into inflationary presssures. "This was obviously not the case," Bernard said. \par \par \uc2  Bernard's comments came as the dollar rose above 103 yen due to apparent Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from just under that level. Traders said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  appeared to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times. \par \par \uc2  The euro hit record lows of 102.48 against the yen and 1.0076 to the dollar in New York trade on Friday, but was trading higher at 104.84/92 and 1.0150/55 respectively in early Tokyo on Monday. \par \par \uc2  ((Tokyo newsroom (813) 3432-8022 Tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbt095ym\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
