\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro hits life lows, brakes fall above parity. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Elizabeth Lazarowitz \par \uc2 790 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 1999\par 22:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Nov 29 (Reuters) - Europe's battle-weary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  fell to lifetime lows against the dollar and yen in New York \par \par \uc2  trading on Monday, treading ever closer to the psychologically \par \par \uc2  key one-to-one level with the dollar before selling slowed. \par \par \uc2  The euro tumbled as low as $1.0038 and 102.34 yen in \par \par \uc2  morning trade as investors unloaded the new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid \par \par \uc2  growing concern that the 11-nation euro-zone is making only \par \par \uc2  sluggish progress in reforming its economies and companies. \par \par \uc2  America's red-hot economy, and hopes that Japan's economy \par \par \uc2  is on the road to recovery also acted as magnets for funds, \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  By the end of trading, the euro was off over half a percent \par \par \uc2  against the dollar but was very modestly higher against the yen \par \par \uc2  compared with Friday's closing prices. \par \par \uc2  Selling dried up in the afternoon after a morning of \par \par \uc2  choppy, nervous trading but dealers said this marks only a \par \par \uc2  temporary reprieve for the euro as investors are still eager to \par \par \uc2  push the euro to parity, likely before year-end. \par \par \uc2  The euro found its footing in late morning trade when \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg warned that \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains a "potential weapon". \par \par \uc2  Only a few weeks ago rampant speculation about the ECB's \par \par \uc2  views on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the levels at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  may decide to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped push the euro higher and lower. \par \par \uc2  But there has been little fresh talk of ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \par \par \uc2  dealers said, even after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold yen for dollars \par \par \uc2  and euros overnight in order to stem the yen's sharp gains. \par \par \uc2  "I think the ECB is pretty comfortable with the way things \par \par \uc2  are," said Henry Willmore, senior economist at Barclays \par \par \uc2  Capital. "They're trying to promote export-led growth, so it \par \par \uc2  wouldn't make sense for them to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  With parity nearly in reach, dealers predicted there may be \par \par \uc2  more losses ahead. \par \par \uc2  "You have to come up with a very creative response (to the \par \par \uc2  euro's decline). They didn't," said Paul Podolsky, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  strategist at BankBoston. "That's going to make it crystal \par \par \uc2  clear they're not going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro, which \par \par \uc2  gives people a little more enthusiasm to sell it." \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg testified before the European Parliament and \par \par \uc2  offered a brighter medium-term outlook, saying the euro can \par \par \uc2  only go higher and that growth in the euro region would outpace \par \par \uc2  growth in the U.S. in two year's time. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, the dollar\tab   managed to find its footing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par against the Japanese yen, erasing its overnight losses to end\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with gains of more than half a percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers remained on guard for more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa confirmed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had bought dollars and sold yen in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market during Asian trading hours.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo is concerned the soaring yen could hurt Japan's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fledgling recovery by raising the price of exports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Nonetheless, dealers still see more yen gains ahead. "It's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par relentless," said Fortis vice president John Schein of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen's seemingly uncontainable strength.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "I have a very good feeling this thing is going to go to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 101, if this continues," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par While the Bank of Japan acted in the market it did so on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its own and dealers were sceptical there would be any help from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe or the United States in the coming sessions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "A real coordinated effort, a massive effort -- this is the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par only way you would have some effectiveness, and only on a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par temporary basis," Fortis' Schein said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Following the euro's lead, the Swiss franc\tab     also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pared its losses against the dollar, but only after slumping to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a decade-low of 1.5975 per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 2134 GMT.  All data taken from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par .\tab \tab \tab     Last   US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1998 Cls\par .\tab \tab \tab \tab \tab 26 Nov.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab    1.0096   1.0164   -0.67  -13.86   1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab     102.32   101.75   +0.56   -9.61   113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab    103.36   103.28   +0.08  -21.60   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab   1.5876   1.5772   +0.66  +15.59   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab     1.6058   1.6063   -0.03   -2.91   1.6539\par Can/dlr\tab \tab     1.4738   1.4681   +0.39   -3.64   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab     0.6375   0.6346   +0.46   +4.25   0.6115\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab  1.6035   1.6023   +0.07   -0.52   1.6119\par Euro/stg\tab \tab    0.6279   0.6321   -0.66  -10.57   0.7021\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212-859-1868)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbt094ok\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
