\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro hits life lows and ends U.S. day mixed. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Elizabeth Lazarowitz \par \uc2 853 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 1999\par 23:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      NEW YORK, Nov 29 (Reuters) - Europe's battle-weary \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  fell to lifetime lows against the dollar and yen in New York \par \par \uc2  trading on Monday, treading ever closer to the one-to-one level \par \par \uc2  with the dollar before selling slowed. \par \par \uc2  The euro tumbled as low as $1.0038 and 102.34 yen in \par \par \uc2  morning trade as investors unloaded the new \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid \par \par \uc2  growing concern that the 11-nation euro-zone is making only \par \par \uc2  sluggish progress in reforming its economies and companies. \par \par \uc2  America's red-hot economy, and hopes that Japan's economy \par \par \uc2  is on the road to recovery, also acted as magnets for funds, \par \par \uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At the end of New York trading, the euro stood at $1.0093, \par \par \uc2  off nearly three quarters of a percent from $1.0164 late on \par \par \uc2  Friday. But against the yen, the euro was up very modestly, at \par \par \uc2  103.37 yen versus 103.28 at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  Selling dried up in the afternoon after a morning of \par \par \uc2  choppy, nervous trading. Dealers said this marks only a \par \par \uc2  temporary reprieve for the euro as investors are eager to push \par \par \uc2  the euro to parity with the dollar, likely before year-end. \par \par \uc2  The euro found its footing in late morning trade when \par \par \uc2  European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg warned \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains a "potential weapon". \par \par \uc2  Only a few weeks ago, rampant speculation about the ECB's \par \par \uc2  views on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the levels at which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  may decide to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped push the euro higher and lower. \par \par \uc2  But there has been little fresh talk of ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \par \par \uc2  dealers said, even after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold yen for dollars \par \par \uc2  and euros overnight in order to stem the yen's sharp gains. \par \par \uc2  Treasury Secretary Lawrence Summers late on Monday said the \par \par \uc2  U.S. dollar policy remains unchanged and that a strong dollar \par \par \uc2  is still in the national best interest. He added the \par \par \uc2  administration was keeping an eye on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \par \par \uc2  developments. \par \par \uc2  "I think the ECB is pretty comfortable with the way things \par \par \uc2  are," said Henry Willmore, senior economist at Barclays \par \par \uc2  Capital. "They're trying to promote export-led growth, so it \par \par \uc2  wouldn't make sense for them to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2      With parity nearly in reach, dealers predicted there may be \par \par \uc2  more losses ahead. \par \par \uc2      "You have to come up with a very creative response (to the \par \par \uc2  euro's decline). They didn't," said Paul Podolsky, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  strategist at BankBoston. "That's going to make it crystal \par \par \uc2  clear they're not going to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro, which \par \par \uc2  gives people a little more enthusiasm to sell it." \par \par \uc2  Duisenberg testified before the European Parliament and \par \par \uc2  offered a brighter medium-term outlook, saying the euro can \par \par \uc2  only go higher and that growth in the euro region would outpace \par \par \uc2  growth in the U.S. in two year's time. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the dollar managed to find its footing against \par \par \uc2  the Japanese yen, JPY=) erasing its overnight losses to end at \par \par \uc2  102.33 yen, up more than half a percent from 101.75 yen at \par \par \uc2  Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  Dealers remained on guard for more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2  bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought dollars and sold yen in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  market during Asian trading hours. \par \par \uc2      Tokyo is concerned the soaring yen could hurt Japan's \par \par \uc2  fledgling recovery by raising the price of exports. \par \par \uc2      Nonetheless, dealers still see more yen gains ahead. "It's \par \par \uc2  relentless," said Fortis vice president John Schein of the \par \par \uc2  yen's seemingly uncontainable strength. \par \par \uc2      "I have a very good feeling this thing is going to go to \par \par \uc2  101, if this continues," he added. \par \par \uc2      While the Bank of Japan acted in the market it did so on \par \par \uc2  its own and dealers were sceptical there would be any help from \par \par \uc2  Europe or the United States in the coming sessions. \par \par \uc2      "A real coordinated effort, a massive effort -- this is the \par \par \uc2  only way you would have some effectiveness, and only on a \par \par \uc2  temporary basis," Fortis' Schein said. \par \par \uc2      Following the euro's lead, the Swiss franc CHF=)   also pared \par \par \uc2  its losses against the dollar, but only after slumping to a \par \par \uc2  decade-low of 1.5975 per dollar. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 2208GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.close at \par \par \uc2  2130GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    US Close US Close  %Chg   YTD %  1998\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Cls\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab    29 Nov.  26 Nov.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab 1.0093   1.0164   -0.70  -13.28   1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab  102.33   101.75   +0.57  -13.28   113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab 103.37   103.28   +0.09  -10.11   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab      1.5875   1.5772   +0.65  +14.83   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab  1.6064   1.6063   +0.01   -2.88   1.6539\par Dlr/can\tab \tab  1.4734   1.4681   +0.36   -4.01   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab  0.6371   0.6346   +0.39   +3.78   0.6115\par Euro/swiss\tab     1.6034   1.6023   +0.07   -0.60   1.6119\par Euro/stg\tab \tab 0.6279   0.6321   -0.66   -9.97   0.7021.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbt0948j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
