\par\par \b \uc2  TRADE IDEA - Buy Bund calls on BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 -HSBC. \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 1999\par 18:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 29 (Reuters) - Investors should buy a call spread on Bund futures because the market tends to bounce after Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, analysts at HSBC said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  They said the January Bund 107/108 call spread could be bought for around 10 ticks, and if Bunds made gains in the next few weeks this could widen to 17 or 34 ticks. \par \par \uc2  "On occasions (of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on January 12 and June 14) we saw a good bounce over the next week of around two full points," said Richard Adcock, manager of technical analysis at HSBC. \par \par \uc2  "With the current position of the Bund market looking fairly fragile we look for a short-term option strategy to take advantage of any bounce whilst having a limited downside," he said. \par \par \uc2  The price gains in Bunds could be attributed to renewed investor confidence once \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were more stable. \par \par \uc2  Adcock said price gains in the Bund future of 100 ticks over the next week would see the call spread worth 17 ticks, and 34 ticks if it gets to 107.00 during the next two weeks. \par \par \uc2  Japanese government officials on Monday confirmed that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars against the yen. The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment on talk from Tokyo bankers that the BOJ was seen buying euros for yen. \par \par \uc2  However, dollar/yen rejected post-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  highs and the euro also fell further to set new lifetime lows against the dollar and yen. \par \par \uc2  Although the Bund future was down on Monday, Adcock said it could still rise on a one-to two-week horizon. \par \par \uc2  ((Aline van Duyn, London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6176, fax +44 171 542 5285, aline.vanduyn@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbt093bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
