\par\par \b \uc2  MOF's Mizoguchi declines comment on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 1999\par 02:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 29 (Reuters) - Senior \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official Zembei Mizoguchi declined comment on Monday on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market talk that the Tokyo authorities had sold yen for dollars in the market to curb the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise. \par \par \uc2  Asked if the authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mizoguchi, the MOF International Bureau chief, said: "No comment, but there is no change in our position that we will closely watch market conditions and respond as appropriate." \par \par \uc2  He was speaking briefly to reporters as he left a meeting at the office of Haruhiko Kuroda, vice minister for international affairs, which was also attended by the head of the ministry's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and money market division. \par \par \uc2  The three men are the key players in conducting any \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa last week gave his deputies the go-ahead to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as needed. \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi, asked what he had discussed with Kuroda, said he had reported to him on his weekend trip, accompanying Prime Minister Keizo Obuchi to a summit of East and Southeast Asian leaders in Manila. \par \par \uc2  Asked if they discussed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Mizoguchi said only: "We are now closely watching the market." \par \par \uc2  Shortly before his comments, traders said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which acts on behalf of the MOF, had apparently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling yen for dollars. The dollar, which was trading below 103 yen in early Tokyo trading, bounced nearly to 104 yen amid the interevention talk. ((Ami Miyazaki, Tokyo newsroom +81-3 3432-8022 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbt0932e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
