\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen surfs higher as yen bulls challenge BOJ. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lisa Jucca \par \uc2 601 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 November 1999\par 14:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 29 (Reuters) - The yen was on the advance against the dollar and the euro on Monday despite the risk that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the foreign exchanges as it did in Asian trading. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa confirmed earlier that the BOJ had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  during Asian trading to buy dollars against yen for the first time in two months, but the yen had more than reversed the losses suffered after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders were looking to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's resolve even though the yen's proximity to all-time peaks around 102.40 against the euro and the psychological 100 dollar/yen threshold was seen increasing the chances of a new round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  But if the BOJ was to act on its own again as seemed likely after a batch of comments by European central bankers, this would do little to reduce the market appetite for yen, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The market seems to be convinced that if we get an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  it will just be unilateral from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Jeremy Hawkins, chief economic adviser at Bank of America in London. \par \par \uc2  "In this context it looks like the yen can quickly approach the 100 level against the dollar and the euro." \par \par \uc2  The dollar was within half a yen of four-year lows around 101.25 set on Friday having backed off an Asian high above 104. \par \par \uc2  Euro/yen was less than a yen above the life low of 102.41 set on Friday according to Reuters Graphics, having shed more than 20 percent against the yen since its launch on January 4. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile the euro hovered within half a cent of its Friday's $1.0073 life low and still within reach of parity against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  BOJ 'SOLO' \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  SEEN INEFFECTIVE \par \par \uc2  Traders said that if the BOJ contined to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on its own, the yen would suffer only short-lived losses against the euro and the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The market is waiting for them (the Bank of Japan) to come in to sell it again," said a trader at Japanese bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "The BOJ are pretty open that they are not trying to put a bottom on it, they are just trying to slow it down. Unless they come in and do something really drastic, which doesn't seem to be their policy at the moment, then after the dust has settled people will look to sell (euro/yen and dollar/yen) again." \par \par \uc2  The euro had started to falter across the board early in Europe after Bundesbank council member Klaus-Dieter Kuehbacher said it could test parity with the dollar on Monday and eased further after ECB's council member Klaus Liebscher was quoted as saying he was "not a great supporter" of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that given the ECB's apparent reluctance to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , chances were that both euro/dollar and euro/yen could head lower. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. Federal Reserve, which was last in the market in July when it sold yen against dollar on behalf of the BOJ, was also seen not to be keen on participating in a coordinated dollar/yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  given the current strength of the dollar against the euro. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the market would take a keen interest in ECB President Wim Duisenberg's comments on the euro when he appears before the European Parliament's economic and monetary affairs committee at 1400 GMT. \par \par \uc2  ((Lisa Jucca, London Capital Markets 0171 542 6745, elisabetta.jucca@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbt091vd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
