\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro stares at dollar parity, recoils. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Elizabeth Lazarowitz \par \uc2 810 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 1999\par 23:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      NEW YORK, Nov 26 (Reuters) - The European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped back \par \par \uc2  from the brink of parity with the dollar on Friday after fresh worries \par \par \uc2  about Europe's economic comeback sent the euro tumbling to lifetime lows. \par \par \uc2      The Japanese yen, meanwhile, surged to four-year highs against the \par \par \uc2  dollar and hit a record peak against the euro. \par \par \uc2      By the New York close of trade, the battered euro had clawed back most \par \par \uc2  of the day's losses, after tumbling to a record low of $1.0076. \par \par \uc2      But market analysts said the fledgling euro -- which will mark its \par \par \uc2  first birthday on Jan. 4 - is not out of danger yet and will likely test \par \par \uc2  the psychologically significant one-on-one level with the dollar in the \par \par \uc2  near term. \par \par \uc2  "I didn't think (the euro) would fall to parity, but now it's \par \par \uc2  inevitable. It's like a magnet that's drawing people to it," said Mark \par \par \uc2  Chandler, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Mellon Bank. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood at $1.0164 as U.S. trade ended, down from \par \par \uc2  $1.0185 in late Thursday trading when U.S. markets were closed for the \par \par \uc2  Thanksgiving holiday. \par \par \uc2  Despite its gains against the euro, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell sharply \par \par \uc2  against the Japanese yen to its lowest since December 1995, shedding more \par \par \uc2  than three yen from overnight peaks. \par \par \uc2      Thin, post-holiday trading helped exaggerate \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves, \par \par \uc2  triggering a round of stop-loss orders to sell dollars. \par \par \uc2      "(The dollar is) just getting absolutely crushed," said Brendon \par \par \uc2  McCarthy, junior yen dealer at Sumitomo Bank New York. \par \par \uc2      The yen also skyrocketed to a fresh lifetime peak of 102.48 against \par \par \uc2  the euro. By late U.S. trading, the euro had pared some of its losses, but \par \par \uc2  still stood some three yen down on the day. \par \par \uc2      "The critical level when this all seemed to happen was 104.50 in \par \par \uc2  euro/yen. Once we broke that, everything just started collapsing," \par \par \uc2  McCarthy added. \par \par \uc2      But late afternoon in New York, however, trading volumes had dried to \par \par \uc2  a trickle as some dealers headed home early after a shortened day in U.S. \par \par \uc2  bond and stock markets. Many banks were already working with skeleton \par \par \uc2  staffs. \par \par \uc2  The euro was dented overnight when conflicting signals from European \par \par \uc2  officials over whether they were willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to limit the euro's \par \par \uc2  slide raised dealers' doubts about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \par \par \uc2  Friday. \par \par \uc2  But market analysts said the rapid speed of the euro's decline and the \par \par \uc2  yen's powerful ascent has helped heighten expectations of action by the \par \par \uc2  ECB or the Bank of Japan going forward. \par \par \uc2  "I still think the probability is still pretty low, but central \par \par \uc2  bankers in Europe are probably getting a bit concerned at the level we're \par \par \uc2  at now," said Jim McCormick, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan. \par \par \uc2  ECB President Wim Duisenburg was quoted in Friday's Financial Times \par \par \uc2  newspaper as saying he would be concerned if the euro fell any further, \par \par \uc2  which briefly buoyed the euro. \par \par \uc2      But ECB board member Domingo Solans said that the bank had no \par \par \uc2  intention of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro. \par \par \uc2      Japanese officials seemed more concerned, however, and \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance \par \par \uc2  Minister Kiichi Miyazawa ordered his ministry to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed. \par \par \uc2      The euro has fallen about 14 percent since its birth as investors pull \par \par \uc2  money out of Europe to buy into Japan, where the nascent recovery is \par \par \uc2  fuelling a strong stock market rally, and bubbling U.S. stocks. \par \par \uc2      One factor contributing to ebbing confidence in Europe is the latest \par \par \uc2  round of government involvement in corporate restructurings, which \par \par \uc2  strategists say could stymie the 11-nation euro zone's economic rebound. \par \par \uc2      Germany's Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder this week helped pull giant \par \par \uc2  construction firm Philipp Holzmann AG from bankruptcy in order to save \par \par \uc2  tens of thousands of jobs. And Schroeder has said he opposes a hostile bid \par \par \uc2  for Mannesmann AG by Britain's Vodafone AirTouch Plc, though he doesn't \par \par \uc2  oppose a friendly takeover. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 2200GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. \par \par \uc2  close at 2130GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab US Close US Close %Chg    YTD %  1998 Close\par \tab \tab \tab 26 Nov.  25 Nov.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par Euro/dlr\tab \tab   1.0164   1.0185   -0.21   -13.10   1.1721\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab    101.75   104.27   -2.42   -13.10   113.20\par Euro/yen\tab \tab   103.28   106.21   -2.76    -7.89   131.84\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab  1.5772   1.5698   +0.47   +14.29   1.3735\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab    1.6063   1.6125   -0.38    -2.50   1.6539\par Dlr/can\tab \tab    1.4681   1.4662   +0.13    -4.14   1.5295\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab    0.6346   0.6360   -0.22    +4.01   0.6115\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/swiss   1.6023   1.6000   +0.14    -0.74   1.6119\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/stg\tab \tab   0.6346   0.6360   -0.22    -9.41   0.7021.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbq0993g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
