\par\par \b \uc2  Bond Markets-Bund price falls pull others down. \b0\par\par\uc2 551 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 1999\par 18:51\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 26 (Reuters) - Falls in euro zone government bond prices triggered by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness pulled prices lower in other debt markets, traders said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The euro's fall to new life time lows and the yen's rise to close to four-year highs versus the dollar were the focus for debt market players, in a session with no significant economic data and with relatively low liquidity due to U.S. holidays. \par \par \uc2  Bond market yields have been rising in the last two weeks and ended this week on a poor note too. Worries about inflation building up, potentially requiring rate rises in the U.S. and Europe, have spooked investors. \par \par \uc2  On Friday, the impact of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves on asset allocation decisions was the driving force. \par \par \uc2  "The euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is continuing to put pressure on bonds. There is a certain level which is deemed to be too weak, and we're very much in that zone now," said Phyllis Reed, strategist at Barclays Capital Markets. \par \par \uc2  "The U.S. came under some pressure which was mainly European driven." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 1725 GMT, the December T-bond future\tab   was down 10/32 at 112-19, with the Bund future\tab     down 0.44 at 105.46.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Falls in the euro, which came very close to parity to the dollar at $1.0076, are seen as potentially triggering liquidations of euro debt holdings by foreign investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese investors in particular have significant euro debt portfolios. But European investors switching out of the euro zone into the U.S. was also happening.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A Reuters poll of European fund managers showed European investors were increasing their weightings of U.S. bonds at the expense of euro zone debt, partly on expectations of further euro weakness and a still subdued U.S. inflationary outlook.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The major story is still the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , after the yen appreciated so much there were many rumours in the market that Japanese accounts want to sell their assets," said Matthias Fachinger, head of Bunds trading at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said he had already seen some selling on Friday, and if the yen's rise was not curbed by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  early next week then further liquidations might continue.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Everyone is eyeing the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to see if they're going to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Fachinger said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par This is how major world bond markets looked at 1745 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Friday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     UNITED STATES -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Futures: December T-bonds 112-20/32, down   09/32\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab    December Eurodollars 93.968, down 0.015\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Cash: Long bond at  98-18/32, down   09/32, yield 6.231 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     EURO -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Futures: December Bunds on Eurex 105.46, down 0.43\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab    March Euribor 96.405, down 0.005\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Cash:    10-year Bund 101.30, down 0.30 yield 5.200 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BRITAIN -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Futures: December Long gilts on LIFFE 108.20, up 0.09\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab    March short sterling 93.690, down 0.040\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Cash:    10-year gilt 103.52, down 0.02 yield 5.293 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     JAPAN -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Futures: March JGBs on LIFFE 130.50, up 0.09 from Tok close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab    Dec Euroyen in Tokyo 99.685, down 0.010\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par   ((Aline van Duyn, London Capital Markets, +44 171 542 6176, fax +44 171 542 5285, aline.vanduyn@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbq098i9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
