\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro recoils in the face of dollar parity. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Elizabeth Lazarowitz \par \uc2 824 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 1999\par 22:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Nov 26 (Reuters) - The European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  stepped back from the brink of parity with the dollar on Friday \par \par \uc2  after fresh worries about Europe's economic comeback sent the \par \par \uc2  euro tumbling to lifetime lows overnight. \par \par \uc2  The Japanese yen, meanwhile, surged to four-year highs \par \par \uc2  against the dollar and hit a fresh lifetime peak against the \par \par \uc2  euro. \par \par \uc2  In late U.S. dealing, the battered euro clawed back more \par \par \uc2  than half of its losses, after it tumbled to a new record low \par \par \uc2  of $1.0076 overnight. \par \par \uc2  But market analysts said the fledgling euro -- which will \par \par \uc2  mark its first birthday on Jan. 4-- is not out of danger yet \par \par \uc2  and will likely test the psychologically significant one-on-one \par \par \uc2  level with the dollar in the near term. \par \par \uc2  "I didn't think (the euro) would fall to parity, but now \par \par \uc2  it's inevitable. It's like a magnet that's drawing people to \par \par \uc2  it," said Mark Chandler, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Mellon \par \par \uc2  Bank. \par \par \uc2  The European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood at $1.0155 at 3:00 p.m. (2000 \par \par \uc2  GMT), down slightly from $1.0185 in late Thursday trading. U.S. \par \par \uc2  markets were closed Thursday for the Thanksgiving holiday. \par \par \uc2  Despite its gains against the euro, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell \par \par \uc2  sharply to its lowest since December 1995, shedding more than \par \par \uc2  three full yen from overnight peaks. \par \par \uc2  Thin, post-holiday trading helped exaggerate its moves, \par \par \uc2  triggering a round of stop-loss orders to sell dollars, dealers \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  "(The dollar is) just getting absolutely crushed," said \par \par \uc2  Brendon McCarthy, junior yen dealer at Sumitomo Bank New York. \par \par \uc2  At the same time, the yen skyrocketed to a fresh lifetime \par \par \uc2  peak of 102.48 against the euro. By late U.S. trading, the euro \par \par \uc2  had pared some of its losses, but stood nearly three yen below \par \par \uc2  its session highs. \par \par \uc2  "The critical level when this all seemed to happen was \par \par \uc2  104.50 in euro/yen. Once we broke that, everything just started \par \par \uc2  collapsing," McCarthy added. \par \par \uc2  But late afternoon in New York, however, trading volumes \par \par \uc2  had dried to a trickle as some dealers headed home early after \par \par \uc2  a shortened day in U.S. bond and stock markets. Many banks were \par \par \uc2  already working with skeleton staffs. \par \par \uc2  The euro was dented overnight when conflicting signals from \par \par \uc2  European officials over whether they were willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  to limit the euro's slide raised dealers' doubts about possible \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday. \par \par \uc2  But market analysts said the rapid speed of the euro's \par \par \uc2  decline and the yen's powerful ascent has helped heighten \par \par \uc2  expectations of action by the ECB or the Bank of Japan going \par \par \uc2  forward. \par \par \uc2  "I still think the probability is still pretty low, but \par \par \uc2  central bankers in Europe are probably getting a bit concerned \par \par \uc2  at the level we're at now," said Jim McCormick, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan. \par \par \uc2  ECB President Wim Duisenburg was quoted in Friday's \par \par \uc2  Financial Times newspaper as saying he would be concerned if \par \par \uc2  the euro fell any further, which briefly buoyed the euro. \par \par \uc2  But ECB board member Domingo Solans said that the bank had \par \par \uc2  no intention of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro. \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials seemed more concerned, however, and \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa ordered his ministry \par \par \uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if needed. \par \par \uc2  The euro has fallen about 14 percent since its birth as \par \par \uc2  investors pull money out of Europe to buy into Japan, where the \par \par \uc2  nascent recovery is fuelling a strong stock market rally, and \par \par \uc2  bubbling U.S. stocks. \par \par \uc2  One factor contributing to ebbing confidence in Europe is \par \par \uc2  the latest round of government involvement in corporate \par \par \uc2  restructurings, which strategists say could stymie the \par \par \uc2  11-nation euro zone's economic rebound. \par \par \uc2  Germany's Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder this week helped \par \par \uc2  pull giant construction firm Philipp Holzmann AG from \par \par \uc2  bankruptcy in order to save tens of thousands of jobs. And \par \par \uc2  Schroeder has said he opposes a hostile bid for Mannesmann AG \par \par \uc2  by Britain's Vodafone AirTouch Plc, though he doesn't oppose a \par \par \uc2  friendly takeover. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 2054GMT. All data taken from \par \par \uc2  Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. \par \par \uc2  close at 2130GMT. \par \par \uc2  Last     US Close  % Chg   YTD %   1998 \par \par \uc2  Close \par \par \uc2  25 Nov. \par \par \uc2  ---------------------