\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Euro loses ground, hits fresh low vs yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 1999\par 08:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TOKYO, Nov 26 (Reuters) - The euro continued to lose ground against the yen\tab      in Tokyo on Friday, probing unchartered territory by late afternoon.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro hit a fresh lifetime low of 105.92 yen on speculative offers, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But steady bids in the dollar against the yen\tab   from Japanese operators tempered falls in the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Concerns of possible dollar-buying, yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  kept dealers wary of pushing the greenback lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The downtrend remains unchanged but I don't see a free-fall," a dealer at a major city bank said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro was briefly buoyed in early trade after the Financial Times reported European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  President Wim Duisenberg said he would be concerned if the euro fell further.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But he said the euro's external exchange rate would matter, in economic terms, only if it had a strong impact on euro-zone inflation. "Does the actual movement give rise to concern? The answer is no. It doesn't matter very much."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Thursday, ECB board member Eugenio Domingo Solans flatly stated the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had no intention of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to defend the euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Such seeming nonchalance gave the euro no encouragement, and chipped away at concerns of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "If we take the ECB's comments at face value, it seems difficult for Japanese authorities to persuade the Europeans to agree to taking action to help stem the yen's rise against the euro," the bank dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Separately, ECB chief economist Otmar Issing said the euro's current external value has been strongly affected by expectations for U.S. economic growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He also said central banks should not flag \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , saying: "Central bankers should never give speculators much sleep."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Vice Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda reiterated on Friday that the euro was "too weak", saying its decline was temporary given economic growth prospects for the European Union.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Previously, the ECB \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on behalf of the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (BOJ) on June 18, buying euros for yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar was supported against the yen on bids from Japanese trust banks near 104.00 yen and also from buybacks by Japanese exporters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "It seemed some exporters had hedged too much and were seen buying back dollars," a trust bank dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Elsewhere, the euro was little changed against the dollar\tab   during the Tokyo session despite its falls against the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The BOJ's Policy Board decided to leave monetary policy on Friday, in line with market expectations. ((Tamawa Kadoya, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3 3432 8027 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 0710GMT.  All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par \tab \tab \tab      Last     US Close  % Chg  1998 Close\par \tab \tab \tab \tab \tab   25 Nov.\par \tab \tab \tab      -----------------------------------------\par  Euro/dlr\tab \tab     1.0161   1.0185   -0.24   1.1721\par  Dlr/yen\tab \tab      104.26   104.27   -0.01   113.20\par  Euro/yen\tab \tab     105.88   106.21   -0.31   131.84\par  Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.5752   1.5698   +0.34   1.3735\par  Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.6118   1.6125   -0.04   1.6539\par  Can/dlr\tab \tab      1.4656   1.4662   -0.04   1.5295\par  Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6372   0.6360   +0.19   0.6115\par  Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.6017   1.6000   +0.11   1.6119\par  Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6301   0.6311   -0.16   0.7021.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbq096gr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
