\par\par \b \uc2  Early Tokyo -2: Euro  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Fears Resurfacing \b0\par\par\uc2 378 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 1999\par 02:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  A senior Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  official commented Friday morning on the euro's weakness. \par \par \uc2  Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda reiterated Thursday's remarks that the euro is too weak against the yen and the dollar and that he expects both \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs to strengthen. He also said that the Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy remains unchanged. \par \par \uc2  Although his comments on euro-dollar and euro-yen reflect the ministry's concerns over these two \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs, market players shrugged them off and continued to sell the euro against the dollar and the yen. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers expect the euro to test its new lifetime low of Y105.97 today, especially if overseas players such as short-term speculators emerge to sell euros for yen again during the session. The euro is expected to move in a range of Y105.50-Y106.70 Friday. \par \par \uc2  There is vague speculation that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the euro-yen if this \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair gets too close to Y105, as this is seen as a key psychological level for Japanese players. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the euro is likely to probe its four-month low of $1.0150, possibly during the global session, as weak sentiment towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and euro-zone economic growth remains intact. \par \par \uc2  Despite the lack of euro-supportive comments from ECB officials overnight, dealers don't rule out the possibility of ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the euro-dollar by the ECB if the euro weakens too rapidly. \par \par \uc2  "There is lingering cautiousness among market players that the ECB might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy euros for dollar if the euro falls near its record low," the European bank dealer said. The euro reached an all-time low of $1.0108 on July 13. \par \par \uc2  In the session, the euro is seen moving in a range of $1.0160-$1.0200. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was trading at Y106.54, up from Y106.51 in London late Thursday. The euro was quoted late in Tokyo Thursday at Y106.40. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6132, down from $1.6152 in London late Thursday. Sterling was at $1.6112 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Ron Harui; 813-5255-2929; ron.harui@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvbq0859d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
