\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Edges Up Against Yen But Gains Limited \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nick Shindo \par \uc2 755 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 1999\par 06:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar inched higher against the yen in Asian trading Wednesday as interbank players took profits, but lingering worries about U.S. asset markets and aggressive exporter-related sell orders nipped gains in the bud. \par \par \uc2  The euro drifted slightly lower against the dollar but recovered some lost ground against the yen, yet weak sentiment continues to weigh down the euro, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar came under early pressure against the yen, drifting to a low of Y104.24 at around 2350 GMT after the Dow Jones Industrial Average closed down by 93.89 points overnight, washing out any hope of a swift dollar resurgence. \par \par \uc2  With a dip back into Y103 territory in New York overnight after a 3 week interval above that level reviving worries of possible dollar-supportive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a real test of the dollar's downside against the yen was improbable, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "With questions reemerging about what the BOJ may or may not do providing the background to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading today, players are watching government officials closely for a hint of action," said a Tokyo city bank trader. \par \par \uc2  Remarks by Japanese Finance Minister Kiichi Miyazawa that the government is ready to combat unwelcome swings in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the morning added to this sense of caution. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the yen's rise to the Y104 level, Miyazawa told a regular press conference: "Experts are saying that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to move drastically for the remainder of the year, but we are always ready to take action against abnormal moves." \par \par \uc2  The remark sparked some short-covering by interbank players and Japanese institutional investor, pushing the dollar to an intraday high of Y104.67 at around 0316 GMT, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Some buybacks were also to be expected given Tuesday's Tokyo holiday, they said. \par \par \uc2  "Given that bids typically thin-out during Tokyo holidays some buybacks were to be expected," said a senior dealer at Nippon Trust Bank. \par \par \uc2  But the rebound was short-lived. \par \par \uc2  In a repeat of recent trading patterns, a solid line of offers from Japanese exporters placed a firm lid on any upward charge, this time in the upper Y104 region, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  With Japanese investors, including public funds, buying around the Y104.20/30 level, trade was inevitably sandwiched in a narrow range, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y104.60, above Y104.35 late Tuesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0275, lower than $1.0283 late Tuesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y107.48, up from Y107.30 in New York late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6247, just down from $1.6248 in New York late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  In other news, market players largely shrugged off the release of Japan's unadjusted trade surplus for October, which showed a slower-than-expected decline of 14.4% to Y1.169 trillion, versus a market consensus for a fall of 29%. \par \par \uc2  Although a cut in the trade surplus is in theory yen-negative, given that exports to the rest of Asia are showing a healthy tone, the message for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  is mixed, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "If anything, this shows that the yen's strength hasn't been hurting exports as much as expected," another Japanese trader said. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, reflecting the fact that strong yen worries may be subsiding even further, the Nikkei Stock Average of 225 selected issue topped the 19000 level for the first time since August 1997 as selected technology stocks rallied. \par \par \uc2  The euro rebounded slightly against the yen in what analysts said was largely a technical correction after hitting a record low of Y106.79 overnight. \par \par \uc2  However, gains were limited, much like the dollar-yen, by Japanese exporters who were said to have been caught by surprise in the shift downwards, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Exporters have sell orders in the Y107.50-80 area and this will limited the upside for the rest of the day," the city bank trader said. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, trade in the euro was typically thin in Asia although some support was being found from a lingering rumor that the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost the euro if it remains below $1.0300, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Market players will be hunting for further clues on this issue when ECB vice president Christian Noyer speaks in France at 1930GMT Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvbo085sm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
