\par\par \b \uc2  Euro Hits All-Time Low Vs Yen As Euro Bears Party On \b0\par\par\uc2 366 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 November 1999\par 18:51\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)-  The euro hit all-time lows against the yen and is approaching its historical low against the dollar midday Wednesday as major European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  continue to slump, dragged down by the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At about 1657 GMT, the euro hit a all-time low of Y106.30 against the yen. Its previous record low against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been Y106.76, reached just one day ago. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, euro sellers kept targeting July 13's all-time low of $1.0108 against the dollar. Traders said the move was just a continuation of the euro's fall earlier in London, on its failure to regain $1.0300 in the Asian session. \par \par \uc2  However, after the end of the London sessions, volumes have been very thin as North America prepares for Thursday's national  holiday commemorating Thanksgiving Day. \par \par \uc2  Reports that Daimlerchrysler would prefer to buy Honda rather than take a stake in either Peugeot or Fiat may have been an additional factor. They prompted new fears concerning the euro zone's recovery and added to earlier worries about Germany's commitment to corporate reform. \par \par \uc2  The euro losses helped the dollar gain ground on all cross trades. The dollar tested again its overnight high of Y104.60, while the British pound hit a new intraday low of $1.6115. \par \par \uc2  This pre-holiday bonus for the dollar came right at the close of the London market, with few believing the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  any time soon. \par \par \uc2  "There's a precedence of the ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , buying euros and selling yen last June," said Robert Lynch, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Paribas in New York. \par \par \uc2  "The odds of the ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on BOJ behalf now are the same as ECB \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the Federal Reserve," he said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A continued surge of the stock markets in the U.S. and Japan also\par suggests that capital flows might continue to favor those regions\par instead Europe, which further fuels bearish sentiments toward the euro.\par    -By Umberto Torresan; Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-4384;\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par umberto.torresan@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010826dvbo01ol3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
