\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar firms with stocks after US rate rise. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Lida Poletz \par \uc2 707 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 1999\par 00:03\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Nov 16 (Reuters) - Shadowing bullish Wall Street stocks, the dollar firmed against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday after the Federal Reserve modestly raised interest rates and eased market fears of more hikes to come this year. \par \par \uc2  "We're seeing the market generally follow the performance of the stock market," said Jim McCormick, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at J.P. Morgan. \par \par \uc2  "The initial reaction in the stock market was positive, then it sold off dramatically and now it (has come) back. \par \par \uc2  Euro/dollar is mirroring that to a lesser degree." \par \par \uc2  After briefly swinging into negative territory, Wall Street stocks reversed course and ultimatly closed up 171 points after the Fed raised rates to wipe out the threat of inflation in the buoyant U.S. economy. The federal funds and discount rates were each lifted 25 basis points to 5.50 and 5.0 percent, respectively. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shifted its policy directive to neutral from a tightening bias, signalling this move may have been the last tightening for a few months. \par \par \uc2  "The news is out of the way," said Seth Garrett, global head of spot trading at Credit Suisse First Boston, adding the Fed move had been largely anticipated. \par \par \uc2  "The Fed took back what they did (credit easing) last year, now it's smooth sailing. Now we have to go back to fundamentals, watch the numbers that come out over the next few months, make sure Y2K is not an issue," Garrett said. \par \par \uc2  But some analysts said caution remained in the market about \par \par \uc2  potential hikes next year, pointing to a selloff in U.S. \par \par \uc2  Treasuries. The benchmark 30-year Treasury bond closed down 1/2 \par \par \uc2  point to yield 6.07 percent. \par \par \uc2  The dollar ended New York trade at its highs against the \par \par \uc2  European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at $1.0295 per euro, up more than a \par \par \uc2  third of cent from Monday's closing level. \par \par \uc2  Traders were closely watching weakness in the euro, which \par \par \uc2  was within a whisper of key support at $1.0285. \par \par \uc2  A break of that level could set the stage for a test of the \par \par \uc2  euro's July 13 $1.0104 lifetime low and a run at the \par \par \uc2  psychologically critical parity level, technical analysts \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also up over a full Japanese yen, \par \par \uc2  reflecting overnight gains amid fears that a too-strong yen \par \par \uc2  could derail Japan's economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  A half-yearly report from the Organisation for Economic \par \par \uc2  Cooperation and Development (OECD) said that further yen \par \par \uc2  strengthening risked derailing \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's improving economy and \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be needed to curb yen strength. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's potential gains against the yen would probably \par \par \uc2  be limited to a very tight range due to strong Japanese \par \par \uc2  fundamentals pointing towards a muscular yen, said BankBoston \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Paul Podolsky. \par \par \uc2  Despite gains against European and Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar eased modestly against the Canadian dollar\tab  , amid\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expectations the Bank of Canada would match the Fed's rate hike\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Looking ahead, traders said they would turn their attention\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Wednesday to October consumer prices, which were expected to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise 0.2 percent against a 0.4 percent rise the previous\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar earlier had shrugged off data showing continued\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. economic vigour, with industrial production in October\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recovering from a hurricane-induced dip to rack up its biggest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gain in seven months.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bid prices at 2148 GMT. All data taken from Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with percent change calculated from the daily U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 2130GMT.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par US Close US Close  %Chg    YTD %\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 16 Nov.  15 Nov.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -----------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr\tab \tab     1.0295   1.0329   -0.33   -11.88\par Dlr/yen\tab \tab      105.87   104.75   +1.07   -11.88\par Euro/yen\tab \tab     109.03   108.30   +0.67    -7.46\par Dlr/swiss\tab \tab    1.5559   1.5532   +0.17   +13.08\par Stg/dlr\tab \tab      1.6162   1.6215   -0.33    -1.96\par Dlr/can\tab \tab      1.4618   1.4653   -0.24    -4.20\par Aus/dlr\tab \tab      0.6428   0.6459   -0.48    +5.63\par Euro/swiss\tab \tab   1.6027   1.6051   -0.15    -0.42\par Euro/stg\tab \tab     0.6428   0.6459   -0.48    -8.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212-859-1868)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbg09wmp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shpp