\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar pares gains in thin US holiday trade. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Elizabeth Lazarowitz \par \uc2 717 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 1999\par 16:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, Nov 11 (Reuters) - The dollar ticked off its highs in early New York trading on Thursday, paring gains made overnight after Tokyo's unveiling of a sizable spending package failed to impress investors and briefly buffeted the yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had shot half a yen higher after the Japanese government announced its long-awaited fiscal spending package would total 18 trillion yen, with 6.5 trillion yen in fresh direct fiscal spending. \par \par \uc2  As U.S. dealing got underway, the dollar had already eased back from its session highs against the yen JPY=) to stand below 105, but remained comfortably above 104.63 at Wednesday's close. \par \par \uc2  Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  EUR=) struggled slightly higher after beginning the New York session just off session lows near $1.04. \par \par \uc2  Trading volumes were thin with many trading floors sparsely staffed for the Veterans Day holiday. But stock and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets remained open, and regular trading will resume on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "You probably aren't going to see a great deal of activity in the market because of the holiday," said Mike Malpede, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Refco Group. \par \par \uc2  Malpede said the dollar could drift slightly higher, but that market players were now set to focus on what the Federal Reserve will do with interest rates at its next policy-setting meeting on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The market is divided as to whether the Fed will hike rates by a quarter-point at its November meeting. But they will be particularly attuned to a shift in the Fed's policy stance, which could signal whether the current spate of tightening has ended. \par \par \uc2  New York Federal Reserve President William McDonough said Thursday it should not be assumed that accelerating growth in U.S. productivity, which has sustained inflation-free economic growth in recent years, would continue indefinitely. \par \par \uc2  The dollar had gotten a head-start against the euro overnight from remarks by Dutch \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor and European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Nout Wellink. \par \par \uc2  Wellink said in an interview with Reuters that improving economic climates and rising energy prices meant there was a slight upside to inflationary pressures in the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  Later, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vice President Christian Noyer said the ECB still thought the euro had potential to appreciate, since its monetary policy is based on price stability. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was also firmer against the British pound GBP=) and the Swiss franc CHF=). \par \par \uc2  Going forward, dealers said questions about how Tokyo plans to finance its budget and its ultimate effect on Japan's economic health could help cap the yen. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Vice Finance Minister Haruhiko Kuroda said overnight that the economic package was appropriate to support the economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  He also said that the current level of the yen was too strong, but analysts said the market would not be too concerned about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb that strength for now. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo dealers said the recent firmness of Tokyo share prices, which rose to a 26-month intraday high on Thursday, was likely to lessen the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term. \par \par \uc2  "As long as Tokyo share prices remain firm, I think monetary authorities will refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the yen rises to about 100 yen to the dollar," said Hideyuki Tsukamoto, manager in Fuji Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  department in Tokyo. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 1447 GMT. All data taken from Reuters Graphics, with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par US Close     Last\tab Pct Change  YTD %\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10 Nov.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par EURO/DLR EUR=)\tab   1.0446     1.0415\tab -0.30     -11.14\par DLR/YEN JPY=)\tab    104.63     104.76\tab +0.12     -11.14\par EURO/YEN EURJPY=)     109.19     109.11\tab -0.07\tab -7.46\par DLR/SWISS CHF=)\tab  1.5391     1.5431\tab +0.26     +12.35\par STG/DLR GBP=)\tab    1.6288     1.6223\tab -0.40\tab -1.91\par DLR/CANADA CAD=)\tab 1.4681     1.4665\tab -0.11\tab -4.12\par AUSSIE/DLR AUD=)\tab 0.6425     0.6430\tab +0.08\tab +5.15\par EURO/SWISS EURCHF=)   1.6083     1.6085\tab +0.01\tab -0.21\par EURO/STG EURGBP=)     0.6414     0.6415\tab +0.02\tab -8.63\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((U.S. Financial Markets Desk, 212-859-1639)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvbb004gb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
