\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen losses vs dollar and euro seen limited. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deepthi Wickremasinghe \par \uc2 739 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 1999\par 09:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 11 (Reuters) - The yen was broadly stable against the dollar and the euro early in European trading on Thursday following mild losses overnight on some disappointment over Japan's economic stimulus package. \par \par \uc2  Despite a larger than expected total package of 18 trillion yen ($172 billion), fresh direct fiscal spending, at 6.5 trillion yen, was towards the bottom end of expectations. \par \par \uc2  No key economic data in Europe and a partial holiday in the United States are expected to limit activity in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The stimulus package was very much along the lines of what people expected except that the actual new money is if anything towards lower end of expectations so there was a bit selling of yen, but it has not been a big move in dollar/yen," said Chris Iggo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Capital in London. \par \par \uc2  "More important going forward is how the budget is going to be financed in terms of what it means for new issuance of JGBs and when we get the updated projections from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  about the budget deficit and the outstanding Japanese debt. They are the long term issues which may ultimately lead to the yen weakening." \par \par \uc2  Dollar/yen had risen around 0.75 percent from overnight lows to reach a high for the day at 105.25 by 0816 GMT. \par \par \uc2  KURODA SAYS ECONOMIC PACAKAGE APPROPRIATE \par \par \uc2  Against the euro, the yen had risen about three-quarters of a yen to its highest since Monday just short of 110 yen. "It looks like we could have more activity on the upside today," said Ian Stannard, technical analyst at Chase in London. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/yen has tested resistance at 105.25/35. There is scope to go up towards 105.80 if this level is breached but we would expect dollar/yen to fail at this level and head lower towards the key support at 104.70." \par \par \uc2  Stannard said further support was offered at 104.45, and below there at last week's lows around 103.35/45. \par \par \uc2  Japan's Vice Finance Minister Haruhiko Kuroda said overnight that the economic package was appropriate to support the economic recovery. He also said that the current level of the yen was too strong, however analysts said the market would not be too concerned about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb that strength for now. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo dealers said the recent firmness of Tokyo share prices, which rose to a 26-month intraday high on Thursday, was likely to lessen the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term. \par \par \uc2  "As long as Tokyo share prices remain firm, I think monetary authorities will refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the yen rises to about 100 yen to the dollar," said Hideyuki Tsukamoto, manager in Fuji Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  department in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  In the stock market, the key Nikkei 225 average ended at 18,327.28, off a peak of 18,659.55 set earlier, the highest intraday level since September 10, 1997. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, euro/dollar was in a tight range above $1.0400. \par \par \uc2  "If volumes were not light enough, today is U.S. Veterans' Day and this is likely to maintain the idea that liquidity issues are triggering the adoption of more neutral risk strategies among the investor community," said Michael Lewis at Deutsche Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "With no first tier data in Euroland today the euro is unlikely to be inspired today despite a host of ECB officials scheduled to speak...and the release of the ECB's monthly report at 1800 GMT." \par \par \uc2  ((Deepthi Wickremasinghe, London capital markets, +44 171 542 7792, fax +44 171 542 5285, deepthi.wickremasinghe@reuters.com)). \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 0840 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  Graphics, with precent change calculated from the daily U.S. \par \par \uc2  close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2     LAST     U.S. CLOSE   % CHANGE   YTD % \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.0423   1.0446\tab  - 0.22     - 11.07\par 105.25   104.63\tab  + 0.59     - 7.02\par 109.77   109.19\tab  + 0.53     - 16.74\par 1.5401   1.5391\tab  + 0.06     + 12.13\par 1.6256   1.6288\tab  - 0.20     - 1.71\par 1.4669   1.4681\tab  - 0.08     - 4.09\par 0.6423   0.6425\tab  - 0.03     + 5.04\par 1.6065   1.6083\tab  - 0.11     - 0.34\par 0.6414   0.6414\tab  + 0.00     - 8.65\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvbb003ov\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
