\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar slips from highs vs yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 701 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 1999\par 14:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 11 (Reuters) - The dollar drew back from two-day highs against the yen but extended gains against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the European midsession on Thursday, in thin trading ahead of a partial U.S. market holiday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose half a yen in Tokyo after the release of Japan's economic stimulus package, but those gains mostly ebbed away during the European session. \par \par \uc2  Despite a larger than expected total package of 18 trillion yen, fresh direct fiscal spending, at 6.5 trillion yen, was towards the bottom end of expectations. \par \par \uc2  "There was very little announcement effect for the yen on the back of the budget statement," said Stewart Newnham, senior strategist at State Street in London. \par \par \uc2  "The markets had so much information from Japanese officials beforehand that they had a long time to discount it." \par \par \uc2  Several senior Japanese officials had given indications on the size of the package in the past week, gradually driving up market expectations for the total amount. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading a little below 105 yen at 1230 GMT, from a two-day high of 105.30 set early in Europe. Euro/yen fell to lows near 109, from an earlier high of 109.91. \par \par \uc2  WEAKER YEN GOING FORWARD \par \par \uc2  But analysts said the longer-term impact of the package could be for a weaker yen. \par \par \uc2  "More important going forward is how the budget is going to be financed in terms of what it means for new issuance of JGBs and when we get the updated projections from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  about the budget deficit and the outstanding Japanese debt," said Chris Iggo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Capital in London. \par \par \uc2  "They are the long term issues which may ultimately lead to the yen weakening." \par \par \uc2  Japan's Vice Finance Minister Haruhiko Kuroda said overnight that the economic package was appropriate to support the economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  He also said that the current level of the yen was too strong, but analysts said the market would not be too concerned about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb that strength for now. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo dealers said the recent firmness of Tokyo share prices, which rose to a 26-month intraday high on Thursday, was likely to lessen the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term. \par \par \uc2  "As long as Tokyo share prices remain firm, I think monetary authorities will refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the yen rises to about 100 yen to the dollar," said Hideyuki Tsukamoto, manager in Fuji Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  department in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  In technically-driven trading, the dollar rose to highs above 1.5450 Swiss francs, to $1.04 per euro EUR=) and $1.6220 to the pound. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. data calendar is bare on Thursday, and analysts said they were looking ahead to the release of U.S. retail sales data on Friday, and to the Federal Open Market Committee meeting on November 16. \par \par \uc2  Sixteen of 30 top Wall Street brokerages surveyed by Reuters last Friday expected no change in rates from the meeting. The federal funds target rate is currently 5.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  But the New York Stock Exchange will open on Thursday, despite the partial holiday, and traders said the dollar was likely to find some strength from U.S. asset gains. December S&P futures traded on Globex were up a modest 2.00 points at 1245 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Some markets, including U.S. Treasuries, are closed on Thursday in observance of the Veterans' Day holiday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 1300 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  Graphics, with precent change calculated from the daily U.S. \par \par \uc2  close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2   LAST\tab U.S. CLOSE   % CHANGE   YTD %\par \par 1.0404  1.0446\tab  - 0.40     - 11.24\par 104.90  104.63\tab  + 0.26     - 7.33\par 109.20  109.19\tab  + 0.01     - 17.17\par 1.5454  1.5391\tab  + 0.41     + 12.52\par 1.6218  1.6288\tab  - 0.43     - 1.94\par 1.4665  1.4681\tab  - 0.11     - 4.12\par 0.6424  0.6425\tab  - 0.02     + 5.05\par 1.6084  1.6083\tab  + 0.01     - 0.22\par 0.6409  0.6414\tab  - 0.08     - 8.72\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvbb003la\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
