\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar perky vs European  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 , yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 691 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 November 1999\par 12:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 11 (Reuters) - The dollar rose against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the yen JPY=) on Thursday, in thin trading ahead of a partial market holiday in the United States. \par \par \uc2  The dollar pushed ahead against Swiss franc, euro and sterling in Europe after getting an unexpected half-yen boost in Tokyo from Japan's economic stimulus package. \par \par \uc2  Despite a larger than expected total package of 18 trillion yen, fresh direct fiscal spending, at 6.5 trillion yen, was towards the bottom end of expectations. \par \par \uc2  "The reaction to the package was disappointing for the yen," said a trader from a U.S. bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "We look like we may be stuck in a 103-108 (dollar/yen) range for the rest of the year - nobody wants to buy any more yen until we have got to 110 to the dollar," he added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading around 105 yen at 1045 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "There was a bit of selling of yen, but it has not been a big move in dollar/yen," said Chris Iggo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Capital in London. \par \par \uc2  "More important going forward is how the budget is going to be financed in terms of what it means for new issuance of JGBs and when we get the updated projections from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  about the budget deficit and the outstanding Japanese debt. They are the long term issues which may ultimately lead to the yen weakening." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  NOT SEEN BEFORE 100 YEN \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Vice Finance Minister Haruhiko Kuroda said overnight that the economic package was appropriate to support the economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  He also said that the current level of the yen was too strong, but analysts said the market would not be too concerned about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb that strength for now. \par \par \uc2  Tokyo dealers said the recent firmness of Tokyo share prices, which rose to a 26-month intraday high on Thursday, was likely to lessen the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term. \par \par \uc2  "As long as Tokyo share prices remain firm, I think monetary authorities will refrain from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the yen rises to about 100 yen to the dollar," said Hideyuki Tsukamoto, manager in Fuji Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  department in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  In the stock market, the key Nikkei 225 average ended at 18,327.28, off a peak of 18,659.55 set earlier, the highest intraday level since September 10, 1997. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also broke through resistance levels at 1.5425 francs, $1.0430 per euro and $1.6250 to the pound. \par \par \uc2  "There are no economic releases, and we have holiday trading activity based on technical factors," said Fabio Fraschetti, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Banca Nazionale del Lavoro in London. \par \par \uc2  But the dollar found some strength against the euro from comments from Dutch \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor and European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member Nout Wellink. \par \par \uc2  Wellink said in an interview with Reuters that improving economic climates and rising energy prices meant there was a slight upside to inflationary pressures in the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  The New York Stock Exchange will open on Thursday, despite the partial holiday, and traders said the dollar was also likely to find strength from U.S. asset gains. Some markets, including U.S. Treasuries, are closed on Thursday in observance of the Veterans' Day holiday. \par \par \uc2  December S&P futures traded on Globex were up 3.50 points at 1100 GMT. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 1105 GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  Graphics, with precent change calculated from the daily U.S. \par \par \uc2  close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2      LAST   US CLOSE   % CHANGE  YTD % \par \par \uc2  1.0410  1.0446     - 0.35    - 11.19 \par \par \uc2  105.12  104.63     + 0.47    - 7.14 \par \par \uc2  109.47  109.19     + 0.26    - 16.97 \par \par \uc2  1.5445  1.5391     + 0.35    + 12.45 \par \par \uc2  1.6234  1.6288     - 0.33    - 1.84 \par \par \uc2  1.4672  1.4681     - 0.06    - 4.07 \par \par \uc2  0.6428  0.6425     + 0.05    + 5.12 \par \par \uc2  1.6079  1.6083     - 0.02    - 0.25 \par \par \uc2  0.6406  0.6414     - 0.12    - 8.76 \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvbb003l5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
