\par\par \b \uc2  Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Holds Firm Vs Yen; Focus On US Data \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nick Shindo \par \uc2 724 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 1999\par 06:30\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The dollar edged a little higher against the yen Friday in Asia, but overall the market just wasn't in the mood for big plays right before the release of U.S. jobless data, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The euro rose slightly against the dollar after taking a beating overnight, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  With most players on the sidelines, the dollar was restricted to just a 55 sen range against the yen, underpinned by spates of Japanese institutional buying and capped by exporter offers, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "With the euro's slip-up commanding the spotlight overnight and the U.S. jobless data calling the shots today, dollar-yen trade has been muted," said a trader at a foreign bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Market consensus is that the number of U.S. non-farm payrolls will show a rise in October by 290,000. The data is due out at 1330 GMT later Friday. \par \par \uc2  However, even the non-farm payrolls data may not spur much activity, some said. \par \par \uc2  "With confidence back in U.S. asset markets, I don't expect the jobless data to make ripples," said a city bank trader. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, the yen continues to be supported against both the dollar and the euro on talk that the size of Japan's second stimulus package will reach Y15 trillion, with as much as Y6-7 trillion in "real water spending," or direct fiscal stimulus. \par \par \uc2  While many \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players have already priced in direct spending of Y4-5 trillion, an amount higher than that would weigh on the dollar against the yen, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Furthermore, a serious approach towards Y100 would raise the specter of dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and perhaps even joint action with the U.S. \par \par \uc2  At 0515 GMT (12:15 a.m. EST), the dollar was quoted at Y104.95, above Y104.89 late Thursday in New York. The dollar was at Y104.62 late Thursday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0395, higher than $1.0375 late Thursday in New York. The euro was at $1.0488 in Tokyo Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar found some support against the yen from an article in the Friday edition of the Yomiuri Shimbun, which suggested that the government will ask the Bank of Japan to continue to use "appropriate and flexible monetary policy," dealers said. \par \par \uc2  However, some analysts question whether the BOJ will further ease monetary policy just yet. \par \par \uc2  "While I don't rule out easing if the yen rises very sharply, I don't think the BOJ will ease anytime soon, especially since it just expanded money market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in mid-October," a European bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar should get an additional boost as the year-end draws near: fear of Year 2000 (Y2K) computer bugs. \par \par \uc2  "I predict that the dollar will be back up to Y125 at the end of the year as U.S. investors repatriate funds on the back of Y2K," the foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The fact that the euro rose, then fell as low as $1.0340 overnight in spite of a 0.5% interest rate hike by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, left some players confused. \par \par \uc2  Concerns that the hike may slow down a German recovery, plus the timing of the decision, didn't help the euro, others said. \par \par \uc2  "(ECB President) Wim Duisenberg started talking about a creeping bias (towards a rise in rates) as far back as July... the long interim period allowed the euro-dollar to overshoot," said an economist at Sakura Bank in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  However, with strong euro-zone economic fundamentals still in place, a rate of $1.0700 by the end of the year is still likely, he said. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro clawed back overnight losses, but talk that Japanese insurers haven't fully hedged their euro-denominated assets may lead some inter-bank dealers to sell, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro was quoted at Y109.10, up from Y108.82 in New York late Thursday. The euro was at Y109.73 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Sterling was at $1.6240, up from $1.6219 in New York late Thursday. Sterling was at $1.6445 in Tokyo late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  -By Nick Shindo; 813-5255-2929; nshindo@ap.org \par \par \uc2  1074 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvb507rzh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
