\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar rebounds as yen fails to sustain gains. \b0\par\par\uc2 625 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 1999\par 05:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Nov 4 (Reuters) - The dollar rebounded against the yen by Tokyo midday on Thursday after the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to sustain overnight gains that took it to a peak of around 103.42. \par \par \uc2  Overnight media reports of a Japanese stimulus package topping a higher than expected 15 trillion yen had earlier fuelled yen gains, but by midday most operators said that figure was not enough in itself to propel the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher. \par \par \uc2  "We were just disappointed with the fact that the yen failed to rally again," said a city bank dealer. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar was at 105.03/13 yen\tab   at 0318 GMT after rising briefly to 105.58 yen in early Tokyo trade. It was at 104.90/98 yen in late New York on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Nihon Keizai Shimbun newspaper reported on Thursday an economic stimulus package to be compiled by the government would likely exceed 15 trillion yen, above earlier estimates by senior Japanese government officials of 11-13 trillion yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The report triggered a fall in the dollar in New York overnight to below 104 yen before short-covering emerged in early Tokyo to push it back up near 105 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The market has already reacted too much to past reports on the size of the package," said the city bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Unless the actual figure comes with 20 trillion yen or more, the market may pay little attention on this issue," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The final size of the package is expected to be announced around November 10.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although the report lifted Tokyo stocks on Thursday, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders were cautious to push the yen higher due to fear of possible Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  yen-selling \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the prospect of falling liquidity ahead of the year-end.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Nobody is willing to take unnecessary positions due to the Y2K problem," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The yen's failure to rise substantially above 103.50 yen overnight gave us an impression that any further rally is unlikely until after the next year," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par When the dollar turned its direction, renewed military tension between Iraq and Iran was used as an excuse for buybacks of the dollar for the yen, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Earlier on Wednesday, Iranian opposition forces based in Iraq said they suffered heavy casualties in a explosion caused by a Scud missile fired from Iran, but Tehran denied responsibility.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But that factor was not strong enough to cause further dollar buying, and instead selling by Japanese exporters capped the topside, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Another city bank dealer said more offers by exporters were likely to emerge at levels near 106.50 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the euro, the dollar was little changed ahead of a meeting of the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's governing council later on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro\tab   stood at $1.0483/85 as of 0415 GMT against $1.0482/86 in late New York trading.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The ECB is widely expected to raise interest rates on Thursday, and growing number of dealers now see the bank raising rates by 50 basis points instead of 25 points, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "We've been waiting for ECB's rate hike far too long," said the U.S. bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Either with a rate rise by 50 or 25 basis points, the euro is likely to be sold," he said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A recent Reuters poll of 32 economists canvassed between October 29 and November 1 showed that expectations for the size of the rate increase were split, with 12 predicting the ECB will raise its 2.50 percent refinancing rate by 25 basis points and 14 forecasting a 50 basis point rise. ((Risa Maeda, Tokyo Treasury Desk, +81-3-3432-8570 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvb400r42\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
