\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Euro bolstered by strong data. \b0\par\par\uc2 563 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 November 1999\par 10:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Nov 2 (Reuters) - The euro was bolstered on Tuesday after economic reports from the euro zone reinforced expectations that improving economic conditions in the region would prompt the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise rate this week. \par \par \uc2  The euro posted broad gains as Italy's Purchasing Managers Index rose, showing the manufacturing sector expanded at its fastest since the survey's launch in June 1997. Increases in French and Italian producer prices and an increase in the French October PMI also helped the euro. \par \par \uc2  But analysts said gains against the dollar may be contained as the U.S. dollar was also benefiting from expectations of interest rates hike on the back of strong U.S. economic growth. \par \par \uc2  "The data are showing that the European recovery is well under way and should be supportive for the euro," said Chris Iggo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Capital in London. \par \par \uc2  "But the U.S. dollar is also quite supported given the expectations of rate hike. Things are good on both sides of the Atlantic." \par \par \uc2  He expected the euro to consolidate within the broad $1.05-$1.06 band for the day. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said they were impressed by the improvement in the Italian PMI as Italy had been lagging behind other major euro zone economies. \par \par \uc2  "The ECB council may be less concerned now about the regional discrepancies that we are still seeing at European levels," said Audrey Childe-Freeman, European economist at CIBC World Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  "If they are going to put rates up this week, this would certainly reinforce the case." \par \par \uc2  The ECB holds its fortnightly policy meeting on Thursday. Twenty-six out of the 32 economists polled by Reuters expect the bank to raise the refinancing rate from its current 2.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  A report by a leading German newspaper cited unnamed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sources on Tuesday saying the ECB would hike rates by 50 basis points this week. \par \par \uc2  "The market is already aware that we are going to get a rate hike but the amplitude of rate expectations has slowly and steadily gone up," said Childe-Freeman, European economist at CIBC World Markets in London. "This is helping the euro." \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro was buoyed also against the yen. It stood at 110.36/41 yen \tab at 0843 GMT from Tuesday's low of 109.45 yen and 109.41/61 yen late in Europe on Monday.\par Meanwhile the dollar was holding within a quarter yen from a session high of 105.05 yen\tab   amid lingering wariness of Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said traders feared the BOJ would take advantage of reduced trading volumes on Wednesday, when \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has a public holiday, and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . The dollar was about 1.8 percent above the 3-1/2-year lows near 103.20 yen it set in mid-September.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The pound firmed above $1.6450 against the dollar\tab   after a sharp increase in British house prices was seen enhancing the chances of a rate hike at this week's two-day policy meeting by the Bank of England Monetary Policy Committee.\par A survey by British mortgage lender Halifax showed British house prices jumped 2.8 percent in October, the strongest rise in a decade. Euro/sterling\tab      was steady below 64 pence.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((Lisa Jucca, London Capital Markets 0171 542 6745, elisabetta.jucca@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvb200yim\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
