\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  IN EUROPE - Yen shows strength vs euro, dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 1,078 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 1999\par 17:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Oct 29 (Reuters) - The yen rallied by nearly two percent to one-month highs against the euro and by more than one percent against the dollar on Friday, amid growing investor enthusiasm for the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Renewed confidence in the yen has come gradually, as investors shrugged off measures introduced by the Bank of Japan on October 13 to add liquidity and cap market interest rates, so depressing the yen, analysts added. \par \par \uc2  "What has changed in the last couple of weeks is the realisation by the market that the Bank of Japan's liquidity measures have not proved particularly significant," said David Coleman, chief economist at CIBC World Markets in London. \par \par \uc2  The yen was looking attractive on Friday after the Nikkei stock index rose by more than three percent to its highest since October 13, and it was announced that Japanese unemployment had dipped for a second straight month. \par \par \uc2  Traders said declines in euro/yen provided the trigger for losses in the dollar/yen exchange rate though losses in the euro were curtailed a little below Thursday's low around 109 yen. \par \par \uc2  "The yen continues to be the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of choice," said Steven Saywell, market analyst at Fuji Bank in London. \par \par \uc2  "It seems that asset market players are determining the direction of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The sector is geared up for thinking that Japan is going to offer spectacular returns over the next two years or so. This explains what's happening in euro/yen and dollar/yen." \par \par \uc2  Reuters polls of fund managers and strategists in Britain, the United States, continental Europe and Japan released this week showed investors in all regions increasing exposure to stocks and bonds in Japan. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro\tab      was trading at 109.55/73 yen at 1456 GMT, from one-month lows of 108.95, and from the day's high of 110.96.\par The dollar\tab   was trading at 104.30/40 yen, from lows of 103.99 and highs of 105.28.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar has fallen this week to a low of 103.65 yen, its weakest since a 3-1/2 year low of 103.17 set on September 15.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market is returning to the position it has largely held since June, analysts said, in which expectations of yen appreciation are counterbalanced by fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has sold yen on the open market on at least 10 separate days in the past four months, most frequently for dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There seems to be a lot more buying of yen against the euro than against the dollar, because investors see more prospect of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in dollar/yen," said Coleman.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar made better headway against European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday, rising to one-month highs against euro, Swiss franc and sterling, amid a positive outlook for U.S. assets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Dow Jones Industrial Average gained 1.33 percent to 10,763 points by 1510 GMT, following a 2.19 percent gain on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board member Toshio Miki said overnight \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could be used to counteract a rapid rise in the yen, even if its impact would be limited.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the dollar lost some of its glitter after comments from European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Chief Economist Otmar Issing strengthened expectations of a euro zone rate rise next week, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Issing said the ECB had to take into account accelerating monetary growth in its policy deliberations, though he played down the immediate risk of inflation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Seventeen out of 24 economists surveyed by Reuters on Wednesday expected the ECB to raise its 2.50 percent refinancing rate on November 4.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro\tab   was trading at $1.0494/01 at 1515 GMT, from a low of $1.0435 and from $1.0521/26 in late European trade on Thursday.\par The pound\tab   tracked the euro higher, rising to $1.6410/17 from lows of $1.6329, while dollar/Swiss\tab   eased to $1.5268/82 from earlier highs of $1.5356.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6320, carolyn.cohn@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro\tab      was trading at 109.55/73 yen at 1456 GMT, from one-month lows of 108.95, and from the day's high of 110.96.\par The dollar\tab   was trading at 104.30/40 yen, from lows of 103.99 and highs of 105.28.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar has fallen this week to a low of 103.65 yen, its weakest since a 3-1/2 year low of 103.17 set on September 15.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market is returning to the position it has largely held since June, analysts said, in which expectations of yen appreciation are counterbalanced by fear of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has sold yen on the open market on at least 10 separate days in the past four months, most frequently for dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There seems to be a lot more buying of yen against the euro than against the dollar, because investors see more prospect of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in dollar/yen," said Coleman.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar made better headway against European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Friday, rising to one-month highs against euro, Swiss franc and sterling, amid a positive outlook for U.S. assets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Dow Jones Industrial Average gained 1.33 percent to 10,763 points by 1510 GMT, following a 2.19 percent gain on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  board member Toshio Miki said overnight \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could be used to counteract a rapid rise in the yen, even if its impact would be limited.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But the dollar lost some of its glitter after comments from European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Chief Economist Otmar Issing strengthened expectations of a euro zone rate rise next week, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Issing said the ECB had to take into account accelerating monetary growth in its policy deliberations, though he played down the immediate risk of inflation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Seventeen out of 24 economists surveyed by Reuters on Wednesday expected the ECB to raise its 2.50 percent refinancing rate on November 4.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro\tab   was trading at $1.0494/01 at 1515 GMT, from a low of $1.0435 and from $1.0521/26 in late European trade on Thursday.\par The pound\tab   tracked the euro higher, rising to $1.6410/17 from lows of $1.6329, while dollar/Swiss\tab   eased to $1.5268/82 from earlier highs of $1.5356.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ((London Capital Markets +44 171 542 6320, carolyn.cohn@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvat012k8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
