\par\par \b \uc2  BOJ did not  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  market in October. \b0\par\par\uc2 164 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 1999\par 12:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Oct 29 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) conducted no dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in October, after doing so in September, bankers said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Data released by the BOJ showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) did not conduct any transactions with the private sector during the month through its special \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account. \par \par \uc2  In September, MOF paid 1.05 trillion yen from the account to the private sector. \par \par \uc2  The account is used mainly to fund \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducted by the BOJ on behalf of MOF. Disbursements also include financial transactions between Japan and global institutions such as the International Monetary Fund. \par \par \uc2  The figures include the last two trading days of the previous month, but not the last two business days of the month, as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  settlements are made two days after transactions. ((Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8550 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvat011vc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
