\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Mizoguchi: Can't Comment On  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 162 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1999\par 02:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- The head of the international bureau at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday that the recent appreciation of the yen against the dollar was unwelcome, but that he couldn't discuss the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  Speaking to reporters upon arrival at the ministry, Zembei Mizoguchi said, "I cannot comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...but a rapid rise in the yen is undesirable and we are watching markets closely." \par \par \uc2  Asked whether weakness in U.S. stocks might increase the likelihood of joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the yen's rise, Mizoguchi said that the ministry would cooperate with overseas authorities "when it became necessary to do so." \par \par \uc2  Asked whether he shared the view that the yen's recent rise against both the dollar and euro was excessive, Mizoguchi would only say: "(The ministry's) view on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't changed and appropriate steps will be taken when needed." \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dvas07ll7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
