\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar creeps down vs yen, but scared of BOJ move. \b0\par\par\uc2 611 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Oktober 1999\par 06:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TOKYO, Oct 28 (Reuters) - The dollar took another downward lurch versus the yen\tab   by midday Thursday, jolted by an official's comment that implied the government was unlikely to step into the market unless the dollar goes below 100 yen, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But dealers and investors are reluctant to push the dollar down too fast, still wary of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Japanese monetary authorities, especially after a Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (BOJ) rate checking rumour late on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  By 0307 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 103.96/99 yen from 104.24/34 yen late in New York on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar dipped to a low of 103.88 yen. \par \par \uc2  Knock-out options were seen lurking at strike prices of 103.70 yen, 103.20 yen and 103.00 yen, and dealers expect attempts to break through those points with relatively few banks likely to defend them, another factor pressuring the dollar throughout the morning. \par \par \uc2  Early on, the dollar recovered from a one-month low overnight at 103.72 yen on commercial demand ahead of daily fix by local banks at 0100 GMT. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the dollar was also supported by flight from the euro  , sterling   and the Swiss franc\tab  , moving sharply higher against those \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in trade weighted terms.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Soon after the local fix, the dollar eased on a media report that Economic Planning Agency Chief Taichi Sakaiya is not very concerned with the dollar at 104 yen and that the government would need to take action if the dollar drops below 100 yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The dollar got beaten by large-lot selling from U.S. players right after the commercial fix together with Sakaiya's comments," said a city bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "He made it sound as if (the government) isn't going to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  unless the dollar goes down below 100 yen," the dealer said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Earlier warnings from Japanese Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Haruhiko Kuroda and senior Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (MOF) official Zembei Mizoguchi against the yen's appreciation did not support the dollar much, but dealers said it did reinforce market caution about possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Kuroda's and Mizoguchi's remarks sounded more determined today, and that held us back from building more dollar short positions," said a foreign bank dealer.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Thursday, Kuroda said the yen's rise against both the dollar and the euro was excessive and that the ministry is ready to take appropriate action against any excessive yen rise.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Shortly after Kuroda, Mizoguchi said the ministry would consider an appropriate response to the yen's rise but declined to discuss the possibility of market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mizoguchi said there was no change in MOF's stance that a rapid yen rise was unfavourable.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, some dealers noted the MOF's task was made more difficult in the short-term because of next month's offer of Nippon Telegraph and Telephone Corp (NTT) shares.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said heavy offshore demand will likely generate demand for yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, dealers remained puzzled by the euro's sudden downtrend especially as the euro area money supply growth outpaced forecasts in September, boosting expectations for a near-term European rate hike.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro's mood has been brightened in recent weeks on expectations of an imminent rate hike by the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The euro stood at $1.0513/24 against $1.0512/19 in late New York on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Against the yen it stood at 109.31/42 yen, down from around 109.67 yen in New York. ((Mariko Hayashibara, Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8478 tokyo.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dvas0128e\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\br